        "course": "C16",
        "seq": 437,
        "acip": "LONG 'KHRID DANG 'DRA BA'I DGE BA'I BSHES GNYEN BSTEN SKABS KYANG SDIG DANG MA 'DRES PA'I NGAL DUB KYI NGAN LAS JI 'DRA ZHIG BYED DGOS PA BYUNG YANG GZHAN LA DKA' SPYAD BYAS RABS KYI YUS MI BDO BAR MA ZAD,",
        "wylie": "long 'khrid dang 'dra ba'i dge ba'i bshes gnyen bsten skabs kyang sdig dang ma 'dres pa'i ngal dub kyi ngan las ji 'dra zhig byed dgos pa byung yang gzhan la dka' spyad byas rabs kyi yus mi bdo bar ma zad",
        "english": "My spiritual Friend is here to lead the blind; and in my service of him or her I am obliged to do anything required of me, no matter how exhausting, no matter how distasteful--so long as nothing morally wrong is involved.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"C16\", \"acip\": \"LONG 'KHRID DANG 'DRA BA'I DGE BA'I BSHES GNYEN BSTEN SKABS KYANG SDIG DANG MA 'DRES PA'I NGAL DUB KYI NGAN LAS JI 'DRA ZHIG BYED DGOS PA BYUNG YANG GZHAN LA DKA' SPYAD BYAS RABS KYI YUS MI BDO BAR MA ZAD,\", \"wylie\": \"long 'khrid dang 'dra ba'i dge ba'i bshes gnyen bsten skabs kyang sdig dang ma 'dres pa'i ngal dub kyi ngan las ji 'dra zhig byed dgos pa byung yang gzhan la dka' spyad byas rabs kyi yus mi bdo bar ma zad\", \"english\": \"My spiritual Friend is here to lead the blind; and in my service of him or her I am obliged to do anything required of me, no matter how exhausting, no matter how distasteful--so long as nothing morally wrong is involved.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 33616,
        "course": "EM",
        "seq": 908,
        "acip": "DE YANG CHOS MTHUN GYI RNYED PA LEGS RNYED CIG DGOS KYI, LOG 'TSO DANG SDIG ZAS PHUL BA'I RNYED PA BYUNG YANG NYES RNYED YIN PAR BLA MAS GSUNGS PAS LEGS PAR RNYED CES PA SDIG CHE BA DANG MA 'DRES PA'I ZAS RNYED SLA BA DGOS,",
        "wylie": "de yang chos mthun gyi rnyed pa legs rnyed cig dgos kyi, log 'tsho dang sdig zas phul ba'i rnyed pa byung yang nyes rnyed yin par bla mas gsungs pas legs par rnyed ces pa sdig che ba dang ma 'dres pa'i zas rnyed sla ba dgos",
        "english": "The supplies that we use for our spiritual practice should be good in another sense: they should be obtained in a proper way. As the teachers have said, “Even if someone offers us a gift of food for our practice periods, but that food has been obtained through some wrong kind of occupation or other bad deeds; then actually we've been offered a karmic debt, and not a gift.” And so when we say that you need to find a place where necessities can easily be found, we are talking about a place where you can find support that is not mixed up with any kind of terrible bad deeds.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"EM\", \"acip\": \"DE YANG CHOS MTHUN GYI RNYED PA LEGS RNYED CIG DGOS KYI, LOG 'TSO DANG SDIG ZAS PHUL BA'I RNYED PA BYUNG YANG NYES RNYED YIN PAR BLA MAS GSUNGS PAS LEGS PAR RNYED CES PA SDIG CHE BA DANG MA 'DRES PA'I ZAS RNYED SLA BA DGOS,\", \"wylie\": \"de yang chos mthun gyi rnyed pa legs rnyed cig dgos kyi, log 'tsho dang sdig zas phul ba'i rnyed pa byung yang nyes rnyed yin par bla mas gsungs pas legs par rnyed ces pa sdig che ba dang ma 'dres pa'i zas rnyed sla ba dgos\", \"english\": \"The supplies that we use for our spiritual practice should be good in another sense: they should be obtained in a proper way. As the teachers have said, “Even if someone offers us a gift of food for our practice periods, but that food has been obtained through some wrong kind of occupation or other bad deeds; then actually we've been offered a karmic debt, and not a gift.” And so when we say that you need to find a place where necessities can easily be found, we are talking about a place where you can find support that is not mixed up with any kind of terrible bad deeds.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 24211,
        "course": "GIE",
        "seq": 699,
        "acip": "MA 'DRES PA'I DRAN PA NYER GZHAG GSUM,",
        "wylie": "ma 'dres pa'i dran pa nyer gzhag gsum",
        "english": "We continue on to the three kinds of close awareness which are unblended.  These are said to be “unblended” in that they are unique.  First comes (1) a close awareness that we should eliminate, within ourselves, any attachment to disciples who listen to our teachings with respect; then (2) a close awareness that we should eliminate, within ourselves, any form of feeling offended by disciples who listen to our teachings, but who show us disrespect; and (3) a close awareness which is devoid of either of these feelings, of attachment or offense.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"GIE\", \"acip\": \"MA 'DRES PA'I DRAN PA NYER GZHAG GSUM,\", \"wylie\": \"ma 'dres pa'i dran pa nyer gzhag gsum\", \"english\": \"We continue on to the three kinds of close awareness which are unblended.  These are said to be “unblended” in that they are unique.  First comes (1) a close awareness that we should eliminate, within ourselves, any attachment to disciples who listen to our teachings with respect; then (2) a close awareness that we should eliminate, within ourselves, any form of feeling offended by disciples who listen to our teachings, but who show us disrespect; and (3) a close awareness which is devoid of either of these feelings, of attachment or offense.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 24772,
        "course": "GIE",
        "seq": 1260,
        "acip": "[E165] BZHI PA MA 'DRES PA'I RNAM PA NI,",
        "wylie": "[e165] bzhi pa ma 'dres pa'i rnam pa ni",
        "english": "This brings us to the fourth sub-group here: the unmixed qualities.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"GIE\", \"acip\": \"[E165] BZHI PA MA 'DRES PA'I RNAM PA NI,\", \"wylie\": \"[e165] bzhi pa ma 'dres pa'i rnam pa ni\", \"english\": \"This brings us to the fourth sub-group here: the unmixed qualities.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 27173,
        "course": "GK",
        "seq": 225,
        "acip": "MA 'DRES PA'I MA RIG PA MED PAR THAL, DE 'PHAGS LAM MA THOB BAR DU RGYUN MI 'CHAD DU 'JUG PAS 'JUG SHES KYI 'KHOR DU MI 'BYUNG, NYON YID KYI 'KHOR DU 'BYUNG TSUL MED PA'I PHYIR, /1\\",
        "wylie": "ma 'dres pa'i ma rig pa med par thal, de 'phags lam ma thob bar du rgyun mi 'chad du 'jug pas 'jug shes kyi 'khor du mi 'byung, nyon yid kyi 'khor du 'byung tshul med pa'i phyir, /1\\",
        "english": "Are you saying then that there is no such thing as a state of misunderstanding which is not admixed? Why do you say that? Because this state of misunderstanding is something that engages in an unbroken stream, up to the point that we finally reach the state of a realized being.  As such it cannot occur as an adjunct to those states of consciousness which engage [intermittently] in their respective objects; nor, according to you, can it occur as an adjunct to a negative consciousness. Second reason not to deny negative consciousness",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"GK\", \"acip\": \"MA 'DRES PA'I MA RIG PA MED PAR THAL, DE 'PHAGS LAM MA THOB BAR DU RGYUN MI 'CHAD DU 'JUG PAS 'JUG SHES KYI 'KHOR DU MI 'BYUNG, NYON YID KYI 'KHOR DU 'BYUNG TSUL MED PA'I PHYIR, /1\\\\\", \"wylie\": \"ma 'dres pa'i ma rig pa med par thal, de 'phags lam ma thob bar du rgyun mi 'chad du 'jug pas 'jug shes kyi 'khor du mi 'byung, nyon yid kyi 'khor du 'byung tshul med pa'i phyir, /1\\\\\", \"english\": \"Are you saying then that there is no such thing as a state of misunderstanding which is not admixed? Why do you say that? Because this state of misunderstanding is something that engages in an unbroken stream, up to the point that we finally reach the state of a realized being.  As such it cannot occur as an adjunct to those states of consciousness which engage [intermittently] in their respective objects; nor, according to you, can it occur as an adjunct to a negative consciousness. Second reason not to deny negative consciousness\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 27960,
        "course": "ILL",
        "seq": 641,
        "acip": "GNYIS PA SA GNYIS PA DRI MA MED PA BSHAD PA LA LNGA, SA 'DIR TSUL KHRIMS YONGS SU DAG PAR BSTAN PA DANG, TSUL KHRIMS KYI BSNGAGS PA BSTAN PA DANG, TSUL KHRIMS KYI MI MTHUN PHYOGS DANG MA 'DRES PA'I DPE BSTAN PA DANG, TSUL KHRIMS KYI PHAR PHYIN GYI DBYE BA BSTAN PA DANG, SA'I YON TAN BRJOD PA'I SGO NAS MJUG BSDU BA'O,,",
        "wylie": "gnyis pa sa gnyis pa dri ma med pa bshad pa la lnga, sa 'dir tshul khrims yongs su dag par bstan pa dang, tshul khrims kyi bsngags pa bstan pa dang, tshul khrims kyi mi mthun phyogs dang ma 'dres pa'i dpe bstan pa dang, tshul khrims kyi phar phyin gyi dbye ba bstan pa dang, sa'i yon tan brjod pa'i sgo nas mjug bsdu ba'o",
        "english": "Here is our second division from above, which is an explanation of the second bodhisattva level: Immaculate. This has five parts of its own: a presentation about how, at this level, ones ethical life is completely pure; a presentation of the praises of an ethical life; the presentation of a metaphor to describe how—at this level—ones ethical life is beyond any adulteration by the things that could work against it; a presentation of the divisions of the perfection of an ethical life; and a concluding summary of this level, accomplished by describing its high qualities.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"ILL\", \"acip\": \"GNYIS PA SA GNYIS PA DRI MA MED PA BSHAD PA LA LNGA, SA 'DIR TSUL KHRIMS YONGS SU DAG PAR BSTAN PA DANG, TSUL KHRIMS KYI BSNGAGS PA BSTAN PA DANG, TSUL KHRIMS KYI MI MTHUN PHYOGS DANG MA 'DRES PA'I DPE BSTAN PA DANG, TSUL KHRIMS KYI PHAR PHYIN GYI DBYE BA BSTAN PA DANG, SA'I YON TAN BRJOD PA'I SGO NAS MJUG BSDU BA'O,,\", \"wylie\": \"gnyis pa sa gnyis pa dri ma med pa bshad pa la lnga, sa 'dir tshul khrims yongs su dag par bstan pa dang, tshul khrims kyi bsngags pa bstan pa dang, tshul khrims kyi mi mthun phyogs dang ma 'dres pa'i dpe bstan pa dang, tshul khrims kyi phar phyin gyi dbye ba bstan pa dang, sa'i yon tan brjod pa'i sgo nas mjug bsdu ba'o\", \"english\": \"Here is our second division from above, which is an explanation of the second bodhisattva level: Immaculate. This has five parts of its own: a presentation about how, at this level, ones ethical life is completely pure; a presentation of the praises of an ethical life; the presentation of a metaphor to describe how—at this level—ones ethical life is beyond any adulteration by the things that could work against it; a presentation of the divisions of the perfection of an ethical life; and a concluding summary of this level, accomplished by describing its high qualities.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 31237,
        "course": "ILL",
        "seq": 3918,
        "acip": "SANGS RGYAS KYI CHOS NI, MA 'DRES PA BCU DANG BRGYAD DU GANG 'DOD PA DE DAG GZHAN GYIS MI 'PHROGS PA'I RANG GI MTSAN NYID CAN TE, RGYU MTSAN GANG GI PHYIR NA STON PA LA MA 'DRES PA'I MI MTHUN PHYOGS 'KHRUL PA SOGS MI MNGA' BAS DE RNAMS KYIS GLAGS MED PA NYID KYIS MI 'PHROGS PA STE, THUB PAR MI NUS PA DE'I PHYIR RO,,",
        "wylie": "sangs rgyas kyi chos ni, ma 'dres pa bcu dang brgyad du gang 'dod pa de dag gzhan gyis mi 'phrogs pa'i rang gi mtshan nyid can te, rgyu mtshan gang gi phyir na ston pa la ma 'dres pa'i mi mthun phyogs 'khrul pa sogs mi mnga' bas de rnams kyis glags med pa nyid kyis mi 'phrogs pa ste, thub par mi nus pa de'i phyir ro",
        "english": "The Dharma of the Buddhas, which we assert has those 18 qualities of being unmixed, has an own quality that it cannot be stolen off by others. The reason why this is true is that the Teacher has no nature of being mixed in with things like error, or ideas that would contradict their positions. As such, their teachings cannot be “stolen off,” or defeated—for that simple reason that they cannot be defeated.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"ILL\", \"acip\": \"SANGS RGYAS KYI CHOS NI, MA 'DRES PA BCU DANG BRGYAD DU GANG 'DOD PA DE DAG GZHAN GYIS MI 'PHROGS PA'I RANG GI MTSAN NYID CAN TE, RGYU MTSAN GANG GI PHYIR NA STON PA LA MA 'DRES PA'I MI MTHUN PHYOGS 'KHRUL PA SOGS MI MNGA' BAS DE RNAMS KYIS GLAGS MED PA NYID KYIS MI 'PHROGS PA STE, THUB PAR MI NUS PA DE'I PHYIR RO,,\", \"wylie\": \"sangs rgyas kyi chos ni, ma 'dres pa bcu dang brgyad du gang 'dod pa de dag gzhan gyis mi 'phrogs pa'i rang gi mtshan nyid can te, rgyu mtshan gang gi phyir na ston pa la ma 'dres pa'i mi mthun phyogs 'khrul pa sogs mi mnga' bas de rnams kyis glags med pa nyid kyis mi 'phrogs pa ste, thub par mi nus pa de'i phyir ro\", \"english\": \"The Dharma of the Buddhas, which we assert has those 18 qualities of being unmixed, has an own quality that it cannot be stolen off by others. The reason why this is true is that the Teacher has no nature of being mixed in with things like error, or ideas that would contradict their positions. As such, their teachings cannot be “stolen off,” or defeated—for that simple reason that they cannot be defeated.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 31241,
        "course": "ILL",
        "seq": 3922,
        "acip": "MA 'DRES PA'I NGES TSIG NI CHOS DE RNAMS SANGS RGYAS KHO NA'I RTEN LA YOD KYI, RTEN GZHAN LA MED PAS RTEN MA 'DRES PA'O,,",
        "wylie": "ma 'dres pa'i nges tshig ni chos de rnams sangs rgyas kho na'i rten la yod kyi, rten gzhan la med pas rten ma 'dres pa'o",
        "english": "Why are these 18 called “unmixed”? The point is that these are possessed in the person only of beings who are Buddhas, and are unmixed in the person of other subjects.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"ILL\", \"acip\": \"MA 'DRES PA'I NGES TSIG NI CHOS DE RNAMS SANGS RGYAS KHO NA'I RTEN LA YOD KYI, RTEN GZHAN LA MED PAS RTEN MA 'DRES PA'O,,\", \"wylie\": \"ma 'dres pa'i nges tshig ni chos de rnams sangs rgyas kho na'i rten la yod kyi, rten gzhan la med pas rten ma 'dres pa'o\", \"english\": \"Why are these 18 called “unmixed”? The point is that these are possessed in the person only of beings who are Buddhas, and are unmixed in the person of other subjects.\"}"
      },
