      {
        "id": 283,
        "course": "C01",
        "seq": 283,
        "acip": "DE YANG BTANG SNYOMS SGOM PA LA THOG MAR DGRA GNYEN GANG YANG MA YIN PA'I BAR MA'I SEMS CAN ZHIG LA CHAGS SDANG GI SEMS SNYOMS, DE NAS RANG GI YID LA 'BAB PA'I GNYEN ZHIG DANG , YID DU MI 'ONG BA'I DGRA GNYIS MDUN DU BSAM STE, GNYEN 'DIS KYANG TSE RABS MANG POR DGRAR SKYES TE GNOD PA BYAS, DGRA 'DIS KYANG TSE RABS MANG POR GNYEN DU GYUR NAS PHAN BTAGS TSUL BSAM STE CHAGS SDANG GI SEMS SNYOMS,",
        "wylie": "de yang btang snyoms sgom pa la thog mar dgra gnyen gang yang ma yin pa'i bar ma'i sems can zhig la chags sdang gi sems snyoms, de nas rang gi yid la 'bab pa'i gnyen zhig dang , yid du mi 'ong ba'i dgra gnyis mdun du bsam ste, gnyen 'dis kyang tshe rabs mang por dgrar skyes te gnod pa byas, dgra 'dis kyang tshe rabs mang por gnyen du gyur nas phan btags tshul bsam ste chags sdang gi sems snyoms",
        "english": "The meditation on neutrality goes like this. First you put your thoughts in an even state, free of feelings of like and dislike, by thinking about someone who is for you a neutral figure: neither your enemy nor your friend. Then you imagine that two people are sitting before you: one of your best-loved friends, and one of your ugliest enemies. Next you think very carefully about how the friend has, in many of your previous lives, taken birth as your enemy and hurt you. You think too about how the enemy has, in so many of your past lives, taken birth as your friend and helped you. This puts your mind in the even state, free of feelings of like and dislike.",
        "raw": "{\"acip\": \"DE YANG BTANG SNYOMS SGOM PA LA THOG MAR DGRA GNYEN GANG YANG MA YIN PA'I BAR MA'I SEMS CAN ZHIG LA CHAGS SDANG GI SEMS SNYOMS, DE NAS RANG GI YID LA 'BAB PA'I GNYEN ZHIG DANG , YID DU MI 'ONG BA'I DGRA GNYIS MDUN DU BSAM STE, GNYEN 'DIS KYANG TSE RABS MANG POR DGRAR SKYES TE GNOD PA BYAS, DGRA 'DIS KYANG TSE RABS MANG POR GNYEN DU GYUR NAS PHAN BTAGS TSUL BSAM STE CHAGS SDANG GI SEMS SNYOMS,\", \"wylie\": \"de yang btang snyoms sgom pa la thog mar dgra gnyen gang yang ma yin pa'i bar ma'i sems can zhig la chags sdang gi sems snyoms, de nas rang gi yid la 'bab pa'i gnyen zhig dang , yid du mi 'ong ba'i dgra gnyis mdun du bsam ste, gnyen 'dis kyang tshe rabs mang por dgrar skyes te gnod pa byas, dgra 'dis kyang tshe rabs mang por gnyen du gyur nas phan btags tshul bsam ste chags sdang gi sems snyoms\", \"english\": \"The meditation on neutrality goes like this. First you put your thoughts in an even state, free of feelings of like and dislike, by thinking about someone who is for you a neutral figure: neither your enemy nor your friend. Then you imagine that two people are sitting before you: one of your best-loved friends, and one of your ugliest enemies. Next you think very carefully about how the friend has, in many of your previous lives, taken birth as your enemy and hurt you. You think too about how the enemy has, in so many of your past lives, taken birth as your friend and helped you. This puts your mind in the even state, free of feelings of like and dislike.\", \"course\": \"C01\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 1527,
        "course": "C05",
        "seq": 145,
        "acip": "MCHIMS MDZOD NAS, MDO LAS LAS DGE MI DGE LUNG MA BSTAN GSUM GSUNGS PA LAS DUS RE ZHIG LAS KYI RNAM SMIN YID DU 'ONG BA BDE BA MYONG BA DANG GTAN DU SDUG BSNGAL LAS SKYOB PA MYANG 'DAS THOB BYED NI DGE BA DANG , RNAM SMIN YID DU MI 'ONG BA MI BDE BA MYONG BA NI MI DGE BA DANG , YID DU 'ONG MI 'ONG SKYED PA DE GNYIS LAS GZHAN PA'I LAS NI DGE MI DGE LAS GZHAN PA LUNG MA BSTAN YIN NO,",
        "wylie": "mchims mdzod nas, mdo las las dge mi dge lung ma bstan gsum gsungs pa las dus re zhig las kyi rnam smin yid du 'ong ba bde ba myong ba dang gtan du sdug bsngal las skyob pa myang 'das thob byed ni dge ba dang , rnam smin yid du mi 'ong ba mi bde ba myong ba ni mi dge ba dang , yid du 'ong mi 'ong skyed pa de gnyis las gzhan pa'i las ni dge mi dge las gzhan pa lung ma bstan yin no",
        "english": "The Treasure House of Chim [Chim Jampey Yang's commentary to the Abhidharmakosha] states: Sutra describes three kinds of karma: virtuous karma, non-virtuous karma, and neutral karma. Virtue is that karma which, in the short term, brings you a karmic ripening which is desirable (that is, a feeling of pleasure), and ultimately protects you from suffering (that is, helps you achieve nirvana). Non-virtue is that karma which brings you a karmic ripening which is undesirable (that is, a feeling of pain). A neutral deed, something neither virtuous nor non-virtuous, is that karma which brings you something which is neither desirable nor undesirable. 49 The Asian Classics Institute Course V: How Karma Works Reading Four: The Correlation of Deeds and Their Results",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"C05\", \"acip\": \"MCHIMS MDZOD NAS, MDO LAS LAS DGE MI DGE LUNG MA BSTAN GSUM GSUNGS PA LAS DUS RE ZHIG LAS KYI RNAM SMIN YID DU 'ONG BA BDE BA MYONG BA DANG GTAN DU SDUG BSNGAL LAS SKYOB PA MYANG 'DAS THOB BYED NI DGE BA DANG , RNAM SMIN YID DU MI 'ONG BA MI BDE BA MYONG BA NI MI DGE BA DANG , YID DU 'ONG MI 'ONG SKYED PA DE GNYIS LAS GZHAN PA'I LAS NI DGE MI DGE LAS GZHAN PA LUNG MA BSTAN YIN NO,\", \"wylie\": \"mchims mdzod nas, mdo las las dge mi dge lung ma bstan gsum gsungs pa las dus re zhig las kyi rnam smin yid du 'ong ba bde ba myong ba dang gtan du sdug bsngal las skyob pa myang 'das thob byed ni dge ba dang , rnam smin yid du mi 'ong ba mi bde ba myong ba ni mi dge ba dang , yid du 'ong mi 'ong skyed pa de gnyis las gzhan pa'i las ni dge mi dge las gzhan pa lung ma bstan yin no\", \"english\": \"The Treasure House of Chim [Chim Jampey Yang's commentary to the Abhidharmakosha] states: Sutra describes three kinds of karma: virtuous karma, non-virtuous karma, and neutral karma. Virtue is that karma which, in the short term, brings you a karmic ripening which is desirable (that is, a feeling of pleasure), and ultimately protects you from suffering (that is, helps you achieve nirvana). Non-virtue is that karma which brings you a karmic ripening which is undesirable (that is, a feeling of pain). A neutral deed, something neither virtuous nor non-virtuous, is that karma which brings you something which is neither desirable nor undesirable. 49 The Asian Classics Institute Course V: How Karma Works Reading Four: The Correlation of Deeds and Their Results\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 1576,
        "course": "C05",
        "seq": 194,
        "acip": ",RGYU MTHUN PA'I 'BRAS BU NI, NGAN 'GRO NAS MIR SKYES KYANG RIM PA LTAR TSE THUNG BA DANG LONGS SPYOD KYIS PHONGS PA DANG CHUNG MA MA BSRUNGS PAR 'GYUR BA DANG , SKUR PA MANG BA DANG MDZA' BO DANG 'BYE BA DANG YID DU MI 'ONG BA'I SGRA THOS PA DANG GZHAN GYIS TSIG MI NYAN PA DANG , CHAGS SDANG RMONGS GSUM SHAS CHE BA'O,",
        "wylie": "rgyu mthun pa'i 'bras bu ni, ngan 'gro nas mir skyes kyang rim pa ltar tshe thung ba dang longs spyod kyis phongs pa dang chung ma ma bsrungs par 'gyur ba dang , skur pa mang ba dang mdza' bo dang 'bye ba dang yid du mi 'ong ba'i sgra thos pa dang gzhan gyis tshig mi nyan pa dang , chags sdang rmongs gsum shas che ba'o",
        "english": "The \"consistent\" consequences are as follows. Even if you do manage to escape the realms of misery and take birth as a human, the following respective results occur to you: 1) Your life is short. 2) You don't have enough to live on. 3) You have problems keeping your partner from others. 4) People don't believe what you say, even when you're telling the truth. 5) You lose friends easily. 6) You hear things as bad sounds. 7) No one listens to you. 8) Your personality is dominated by desire. 9) Your personality is dominated by anger. 10) Your personality is dominated by stupidity.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"C05\", \"acip\": \",RGYU MTHUN PA'I 'BRAS BU NI, NGAN 'GRO NAS MIR SKYES KYANG RIM PA LTAR TSE THUNG BA DANG LONGS SPYOD KYIS PHONGS PA DANG CHUNG MA MA BSRUNGS PAR 'GYUR BA DANG , SKUR PA MANG BA DANG MDZA' BO DANG 'BYE BA DANG YID DU MI 'ONG BA'I SGRA THOS PA DANG GZHAN GYIS TSIG MI NYAN PA DANG , CHAGS SDANG RMONGS GSUM SHAS CHE BA'O,\", \"wylie\": \"rgyu mthun pa'i 'bras bu ni, ngan 'gro nas mir skyes kyang rim pa ltar tshe thung ba dang longs spyod kyis phongs pa dang chung ma ma bsrungs par 'gyur ba dang , skur pa mang ba dang mdza' bo dang 'bye ba dang yid du mi 'ong ba'i sgra thos pa dang gzhan gyis tshig mi nyan pa dang , chags sdang rmongs gsum shas che ba'o\", \"english\": \"The \\\"consistent\\\" consequences are as follows. Even if you do manage to escape the realms of misery and take birth as a human, the following respective results occur to you: 1) Your life is short. 2) You don't have enough to live on. 3) You have problems keeping your partner from others. 4) People don't believe what you say, even when you're telling the truth. 5) You lose friends easily. 6) You hear things as bad sounds. 7) No one listens to you. 8) Your personality is dominated by desire. 9) Your personality is dominated by anger. 10) Your personality is dominated by stupidity.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 1577,
        "course": "C05",
        "seq": 195,
        "acip": ",BDEN PA PO'I LE'U DANG SA BCU PA'I MDO LAS NI DE RE RE LA 'BRAS BU GNYIS GNYIS GSUNGS TE, GAL TE MIR SKYES NA YANG TSE THUNG LA NAD MANG BA DANG LONGS SPYOD CHUNG LA LONGS SPYOD GZHAN DANG THUN MONG BA DANG G-YOG 'KHOR MI BSRUN PA'AM YID BRTAN DU MI RUNG LA CHUNG MA 'GRAN ZLA DANG BCAS PA DANG , SKUR PA MANG ZHING GZHAN GYIS BSLU BA DANG 'KHOR MI 'DUM ZHING NGAN PA DANG YID DU MI 'ONG BA THOS SHING 'THAB MO'I TSIG TU 'GYUR BA DANG TSIG MI BTZUN PA'AM TSIG BZUNG MI 'OS SHING MA NGES PA'I SPOBS PAR 'GYUR BA DANG , 'DOD PA CHE ZHING CHOG MI SHES PA DANG MI PHAN PA TSOL BA'AM PHAN PA MI TSOL BA DANG GZHAN LA GNOD PA BYED PA'AM GZHAN GYIS GNOD PA BYED PAR 'GYUR BA DANG LTA BA NGAN ZHING G-YO SGYU CAN DU 'GYUR BAR GSUNGS SO,",
        "wylie": "bden pa po'i le'u dang sa bcu pa'i mdo las ni de re re la 'bras bu gnyis gnyis gsungs te, gal te mir skyes na yang tshe thung la nad mang ba dang longs spyod chung la longs spyod gzhan dang thun mong ba dang g-yog 'khor mi bsrun pa'am yid brtan du mi rung la chung ma 'gran zla dang bcas pa dang , skur pa mang zhing gzhan gyis bslu ba dang 'khor mi 'dum zhing ngan pa dang yid du mi 'ong ba thos shing 'thab mo'i tshig tu 'gyur ba dang tshig mi btsun pa'am tshig bzung mi 'os shing ma nges pa'i spobs par 'gyur ba dang , 'dod pa che zhing chog mi shes pa dang mi phan pa tshol ba'am phan pa mi tshol ba dang gzhan la gnod pa byed pa'am gzhan gyis gnod pa byed par 'gyur ba dang lta ba ngan zhing g-yo sgyu can du 'gyur bar gsungs so",
        "english": "The Chapter on the True and the Sutra on the Ten Levels state that there are two such consequences for each of the ones given here; even if you do manage to take birth as a human, 1) Your life is short, and you get sick easily. 2) You don't have enough to live on, and what you do have is all just common property with others. 3) The people who work around you are \"inconsistent,\" which here means unreliable, and you find yourself having a lot of competition for your partner. 4) No one believes what you say, even when you are speaking the truth, and others are always deceiving you. 5) The people around you are always fighting against one another, and have an undesirable character. 6) You hear many unpleasant things, and when others talk to you it always seems to you as if they want to start a fight. 7) No one respects what you say--no one thinks that what you say has any particular value, and you are afflicted with a lack of confidence. 8) Your personality is dominated by desire, and you are never satisfied with what you have. 9) You are always finding yourself without help, or never find the help you need; and you are always hurting others, or always being hurt by others. 10) You become a person who keeps harmful views, or a deceitful person.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"C05\", \"acip\": \",BDEN PA PO'I LE'U DANG SA BCU PA'I MDO LAS NI DE RE RE LA 'BRAS BU GNYIS GNYIS GSUNGS TE, GAL TE MIR SKYES NA YANG TSE THUNG LA NAD MANG BA DANG LONGS SPYOD CHUNG LA LONGS SPYOD GZHAN DANG THUN MONG BA DANG G-YOG 'KHOR MI BSRUN PA'AM YID BRTAN DU MI RUNG LA CHUNG MA 'GRAN ZLA DANG BCAS PA DANG , SKUR PA MANG ZHING GZHAN GYIS BSLU BA DANG 'KHOR MI 'DUM ZHING NGAN PA DANG YID DU MI 'ONG BA THOS SHING 'THAB MO'I TSIG TU 'GYUR BA DANG TSIG MI BTZUN PA'AM TSIG BZUNG MI 'OS SHING MA NGES PA'I SPOBS PAR 'GYUR BA DANG , 'DOD PA CHE ZHING CHOG MI SHES PA DANG MI PHAN PA TSOL BA'AM PHAN PA MI TSOL BA DANG GZHAN LA GNOD PA BYED PA'AM GZHAN GYIS GNOD PA BYED PAR 'GYUR BA DANG LTA BA NGAN ZHING G-YO SGYU CAN DU 'GYUR BAR GSUNGS SO,\", \"wylie\": \"bden pa po'i le'u dang sa bcu pa'i mdo las ni de re re la 'bras bu gnyis gnyis gsungs te, gal te mir skyes na yang tshe thung la nad mang ba dang longs spyod chung la longs spyod gzhan dang thun mong ba dang g-yog 'khor mi bsrun pa'am yid brtan du mi rung la chung ma 'gran zla dang bcas pa dang , skur pa mang zhing gzhan gyis bslu ba dang 'khor mi 'dum zhing ngan pa dang yid du mi 'ong ba thos shing 'thab mo'i tshig tu 'gyur ba dang tshig mi btsun pa'am tshig bzung mi 'os shing ma nges pa'i spobs par 'gyur ba dang , 'dod pa che zhing chog mi shes pa dang mi phan pa tshol ba'am phan pa mi tshol ba dang gzhan la gnod pa byed pa'am gzhan gyis gnod pa byed par 'gyur ba dang lta ba ngan zhing g-yo sgyu can du 'gyur bar gsungs so\", \"english\": \"The Chapter on the True and the Sutra on the Ten Levels state that there are two such consequences for each of the ones given here; even if you do manage to take birth as a human, 1) Your life is short, and you get sick easily. 2) You don't have enough to live on, and what you do have is all just common property with others. 3) The people who work around you are \\\"inconsistent,\\\" which here means unreliable, and you find yourself having a lot of competition for your partner. 4) No one believes what you say, even when you are speaking the truth, and others are always deceiving you. 5) The people around you are always fighting against one another, and have an undesirable character. 6) You hear many unpleasant things, and when others talk to you it always seems to you as if they want to start a fight. 7) No one respects what you say--no one thinks that what you say has any particular value, and you are afflicted with a lack of confidence. 8) Your personality is dominated by desire, and you are never satisfied with what you have. 9) You are always finding yourself without help, or never find the help you need; and you are always hurting others, or always being hurt by others. 10) You become a person who keeps harmful views, or a deceitful person.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 1699,
        "course": "C05",
        "seq": 317,
        "acip": "[IV.237-40] ,'O NA LAS DE DAG GI NGO BO JI LTA BU ZHE NA, MI DGE BA NI GNAG LA RNAM PAR SMIN PA GNAG PA'I LAS YIN TE, RANG GI NGO BO NYON MONGS CAN YIN PAS GNAG LA, RNAM SMIN YID DU MI 'ONG BA 'BYIN PAS RNAM SMIN YANG GNAG PA'I PHYIR,",
        "wylie": "[iv.237-40] ,'o na las de dag gi ngo bo ji lta bu zhe na, mi dge ba ni gnag la rnam par smin pa gnag pa'i las yin te, rang gi ngo bo nyon mongs can yin pas gnag la, rnam smin yid du mi 'ong ba 'byin pas rnam smin yang gnag pa'i phyir",
        "english": "Just how do we describe these four types of deeds? Non-virtue represents a type of deed which is black and ripens into something black. It is black in that its very nature consists of something afflicted. It also ripens into something black, for it ripens forth into an undesirable result.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"C05\", \"acip\": \"[IV.237-40] ,'O NA LAS DE DAG GI NGO BO JI LTA BU ZHE NA, MI DGE BA NI GNAG LA RNAM PAR SMIN PA GNAG PA'I LAS YIN TE, RANG GI NGO BO NYON MONGS CAN YIN PAS GNAG LA, RNAM SMIN YID DU MI 'ONG BA 'BYIN PAS RNAM SMIN YANG GNAG PA'I PHYIR,\", \"wylie\": \"[iv.237-40] ,'o na las de dag gi ngo bo ji lta bu zhe na, mi dge ba ni gnag la rnam par smin pa gnag pa'i las yin te, rang gi ngo bo nyon mongs can yin pas gnag la, rnam smin yid du mi 'ong ba 'byin pas rnam smin yang gnag pa'i phyir\", \"english\": \"Just how do we describe these four types of deeds? Non-virtue represents a type of deed which is black and ripens into something black. It is black in that its very nature consists of something afflicted. It also ripens into something black, for it ripens forth into an undesirable result.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 2107,
        "course": "C07",
        "seq": 37,
        "acip": "DE YANG BTANG SNYOMS SGOM PA LA THOG MAR DGRA GNYEN GANG YANG MA YIN PA'I BAR MA'I SEMS CAN ZHIG LA CHAGS SDANG GI SEMS SNYOMS, DE NAS RANG GI YID LA 'BAB PA'I GNYEN ZHIG DANG, YID DU MI 'ONG BA'I DGRA GNYIS MDUN DU BSAM STE, GNYEN 'DIS KYANG TSE RABS MANG POR DGRAR SKYES TE GNOD PA BYAS, DGRA 'DIS KYANG TSE RABS MANG POR GNYEN DU GYUR NAS PHAN BTAGS TSUL BSAM STE CHAGS SDANG GI SEMS SNYOMS,",
        "wylie": "de yang btang snyoms sgom pa la thog mar dgra gnyen gang yang ma yin pa'i bar ma'i sems can zhig la chags sdang gi sems snyoms, de nas rang gi yid la 'bab pa'i gnyen zhig dang, yid du mi 'ong ba'i dgra gnyis mdun du bsam ste, gnyen 'dis kyang tshe rabs mang por dgrar skyes te gnod pa byas, dgra 'dis kyang tshe rabs mang por gnyen du gyur nas phan btags tshul bsam ste chags sdang gi sems snyoms",
        "english": "The meditation on neutrality goes like this. First you put your thoughts in an even state, free of feelings of like and dislike, by thinking about someone who is for you a neutral figure: neither your enemy nor your friend. Then you imagine that two people are sitting before you: one of your best-loved friends, and one of your ugliest enemies. Next you think very carefully about how the friend has, in many of your previous lives, taken birth as your enemy and hurt you. You think too about how the enemy has, in so many of your past lives, taken birth as your friend and helped you. This puts your mind in the even state, free of feelings of like and dislike.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"C07\", \"acip\": \"DE YANG BTANG SNYOMS SGOM PA LA THOG MAR DGRA GNYEN GANG YANG MA YIN PA'I BAR MA'I SEMS CAN ZHIG LA CHAGS SDANG GI SEMS SNYOMS, DE NAS RANG GI YID LA 'BAB PA'I GNYEN ZHIG DANG, YID DU MI 'ONG BA'I DGRA GNYIS MDUN DU BSAM STE, GNYEN 'DIS KYANG TSE RABS MANG POR DGRAR SKYES TE GNOD PA BYAS, DGRA 'DIS KYANG TSE RABS MANG POR GNYEN DU GYUR NAS PHAN BTAGS TSUL BSAM STE CHAGS SDANG GI SEMS SNYOMS,\", \"wylie\": \"de yang btang snyoms sgom pa la thog mar dgra gnyen gang yang ma yin pa'i bar ma'i sems can zhig la chags sdang gi sems snyoms, de nas rang gi yid la 'bab pa'i gnyen zhig dang, yid du mi 'ong ba'i dgra gnyis mdun du bsam ste, gnyen 'dis kyang tshe rabs mang por dgrar skyes te gnod pa byas, dgra 'dis kyang tshe rabs mang por gnyen du gyur nas phan btags tshul bsam ste chags sdang gi sems snyoms\", \"english\": \"The meditation on neutrality goes like this. First you put your thoughts in an even state, free of feelings of like and dislike, by thinking about someone who is for you a neutral figure: neither your enemy nor your friend. Then you imagine that two people are sitting before you: one of your best-loved friends, and one of your ugliest enemies. Next you think very carefully about how the friend has, in many of your previous lives, taken birth as your enemy and hurt you. You think too about how the enemy has, in so many of your past lives, taken birth as your friend and helped you. This puts your mind in the even state, free of feelings of like and dislike.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 2664,
        "course": "C08",
        "seq": 319,
        "acip": ",DE LAS KYANG LUS DANG NGAG DANG YID KYI NYES SPYOD BCU DANG MTSAMS MED PA DANG DE DANG NYE BA DANG DAM PA'I CHOS SPONG BA LA SOGS PA MI DGE BA'I LAS NGAN 'GRO LA SOGS PA'I SDUG BSNGAL DRAG PO 'DREN PAR BYED PA LA MTHU PHUL DU BYUNG BA RNAMS NYI MA RE RE BZHIN JE RGYAS SU 'GRO LA, DE DAG GI GNYEN PO LEGS PAR GSUNGS PA'I CHOS KYI BDUD RTZI LA RGYAB KYIS JE PHYOGS SU SONG NAS MNGON MTHO DANG NGES LEGS KYI SROG BCAD DE, NGAN 'GRO SDUG BSNGAL DRAG CING RTZUB LA TSA ZHING YID DU MI 'ONG BA'I GNAS SU, 'CHI BAS NYE BAR BCOM NAS LAS NGAN PAS 'KHRID PAR BYED PAS NA DE LAS MA RUNGS PA'I SGO GZHAN CI ZHIG YOD,",
        "wylie": "de las kyang lus dang ngag dang yid kyi nyes spyod bcu dang mtshams med pa dang de dang nye ba dang dam pa'i chos spong ba la sogs pa mi dge ba'i las ngan 'gro la sogs pa'i sdug bsngal drag po 'dren par byed pa la mthu phul du byung ba rnams nyi ma re re bzhin je rgyas su 'gro la, de dag gi gnyen po legs par gsungs pa'i chos kyi bdud rtsi la rgyab kyis je phyogs su song nas mngon mtho dang nges legs kyi srog bcad de, ngan 'gro sdug bsngal drag cing rtsub la tsha zhing yid du mi 'ong ba'i gnas su, 'chi bas nye bar bcom nas las ngan pas 'khrid par byed pas na de las ma rungs pa'i sgo gzhan ci zhig yod",
        "english": "These afflictions in turn lead you to harmful deeds done in your acts, your words, and your thoughts: deeds like the ten non-virtues, and the five \"immediate\" deeds, and the five that are close to these, and giving up the highest Dharma, and on and on. Every single day then deeds like these, of tremendous power, capable of leading you to the sufferings of the three lower realms and the like, will tend to increase, further and further. The antidote for all these deeds is the nectar of the Dharma, spoken so true, and the further you turn from it then the more tightly you strangle your chances for the higher realms, and ultimate good. Death will rip away your life, and the wrong deeds you have done will drag you to the lower realms, to a fearful place of mighty and savage suffering, to the fires. And so I ask you, where could you find any thought more disastrous for you than this idea, that what is impermanent could be permanent?",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"C08\", \"acip\": \",DE LAS KYANG LUS DANG NGAG DANG YID KYI NYES SPYOD BCU DANG MTSAMS MED PA DANG DE DANG NYE BA DANG DAM PA'I CHOS SPONG BA LA SOGS PA MI DGE BA'I LAS NGAN 'GRO LA SOGS PA'I SDUG BSNGAL DRAG PO 'DREN PAR BYED PA LA MTHU PHUL DU BYUNG BA RNAMS NYI MA RE RE BZHIN JE RGYAS SU 'GRO LA, DE DAG GI GNYEN PO LEGS PAR GSUNGS PA'I CHOS KYI BDUD RTZI LA RGYAB KYIS JE PHYOGS SU SONG NAS MNGON MTHO DANG NGES LEGS KYI SROG BCAD DE, NGAN 'GRO SDUG BSNGAL DRAG CING RTZUB LA TSA ZHING YID DU MI 'ONG BA'I GNAS SU, 'CHI BAS NYE BAR BCOM NAS LAS NGAN PAS 'KHRID PAR BYED PAS NA DE LAS MA RUNGS PA'I SGO GZHAN CI ZHIG YOD,\", \"wylie\": \"de las kyang lus dang ngag dang yid kyi nyes spyod bcu dang mtshams med pa dang de dang nye ba dang dam pa'i chos spong ba la sogs pa mi dge ba'i las ngan 'gro la sogs pa'i sdug bsngal drag po 'dren par byed pa la mthu phul du byung ba rnams nyi ma re re bzhin je rgyas su 'gro la, de dag gi gnyen po legs par gsungs pa'i chos kyi bdud rtsi la rgyab kyis je phyogs su song nas mngon mtho dang nges legs kyi srog bcad de, ngan 'gro sdug bsngal drag cing rtsub la tsha zhing yid du mi 'ong ba'i gnas su, 'chi bas nye bar bcom nas las ngan pas 'khrid par byed pas na de las ma rungs pa'i sgo gzhan ci zhig yod\", \"english\": \"These afflictions in turn lead you to harmful deeds done in your acts, your words, and your thoughts: deeds like the ten non-virtues, and the five \\\"immediate\\\" deeds, and the five that are close to these, and giving up the highest Dharma, and on and on. Every single day then deeds like these, of tremendous power, capable of leading you to the sufferings of the three lower realms and the like, will tend to increase, further and further. The antidote for all these deeds is the nectar of the Dharma, spoken so true, and the further you turn from it then the more tightly you strangle your chances for the higher realms, and ultimate good. Death will rip away your life, and the wrong deeds you have done will drag you to the lower realms, to a fearful place of mighty and savage suffering, to the fires. And so I ask you, where could you find any thought more disastrous for you than this idea, that what is impermanent could be permanent?\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 2876,
        "course": "C09",
        "seq": 151,
        "acip": ",RGYU MTHUN PA'I 'BRAS BU NI, NGAN 'GRO NAS MIR SKYES KYANG RIM PA LTAR TSE THUNG BA DANG LONGS SPYOD KYIS PHONGS PA DANG CHUNG MA MA BSRUNGS PAR 'GYUR BA DANG , SKUR PA MANG BA DANG MDZA' BO DANG 'BYE BA DANG YID DU MI 'ONG BA'I SGRA THOS PA DANG GZHAN GYIS TSIG MI NYAN PA DANG , CHAGS SDANG RMONGS GSUM SHAS CHE BA'O,",
        "wylie": "rgyu mthun pa'i 'bras bu ni, ngan 'gro nas mir skyes kyang rim pa ltar tshe thung ba dang longs spyod kyis phongs pa dang chung ma ma bsrungs par 'gyur ba dang , skur pa mang ba dang mdza' bo dang 'bye ba dang yid du mi 'ong ba'i sgra thos pa dang gzhan gyis tshig mi nyan pa dang , chags sdang rmongs gsum shas che ba'o",
        "english": "The \"consistent\" consequences are as follows. Even if you do manage to escape the realms of misery and take birth as a human, the following respective results occur to you: 1) Your life is short. 2) You don't have enough to live on. 3) You have problems keeping your partner from others. 4) People don't believe what you say, even when you're telling the truth. 5) You lose friends easily. 6) You hear things as bad sounds. 7) No one listens to you. 8) Your personality is dominated by desire. 9) Your personality is dominated by anger. 10) Your personality is dominated by stupidity.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"C09\", \"acip\": \",RGYU MTHUN PA'I 'BRAS BU NI, NGAN 'GRO NAS MIR SKYES KYANG RIM PA LTAR TSE THUNG BA DANG LONGS SPYOD KYIS PHONGS PA DANG CHUNG MA MA BSRUNGS PAR 'GYUR BA DANG , SKUR PA MANG BA DANG MDZA' BO DANG 'BYE BA DANG YID DU MI 'ONG BA'I SGRA THOS PA DANG GZHAN GYIS TSIG MI NYAN PA DANG , CHAGS SDANG RMONGS GSUM SHAS CHE BA'O,\", \"wylie\": \"rgyu mthun pa'i 'bras bu ni, ngan 'gro nas mir skyes kyang rim pa ltar tshe thung ba dang longs spyod kyis phongs pa dang chung ma ma bsrungs par 'gyur ba dang , skur pa mang ba dang mdza' bo dang 'bye ba dang yid du mi 'ong ba'i sgra thos pa dang gzhan gyis tshig mi nyan pa dang , chags sdang rmongs gsum shas che ba'o\", \"english\": \"The \\\"consistent\\\" consequences are as follows. Even if you do manage to escape the realms of misery and take birth as a human, the following respective results occur to you: 1) Your life is short. 2) You don't have enough to live on. 3) You have problems keeping your partner from others. 4) People don't believe what you say, even when you're telling the truth. 5) You lose friends easily. 6) You hear things as bad sounds. 7) No one listens to you. 8) Your personality is dominated by desire. 9) Your personality is dominated by anger. 10) Your personality is dominated by stupidity.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 2877,
        "course": "C09",
        "seq": 152,
        "acip": ",BDEN PA PO'I LE'U DANG SA BCU PA'I MDO LAS NI DE RE RE LA 'BRAS BU GNYIS GNYIS GSUNGS TE, GAL TE MIR SKYES NA YANG TSE THUNG LA NAD MANG BA DANG LONGS SPYOD CHUNG LA LONGS SPYOD GZHAN DANG THUN MONG BA DANG G-YOG 'KHOR MI BSRUN PA'AM YID BRTAN DU MI RUNG LA CHUNG MA 'GRAN ZLA DANG BCAS PA DANG , SKUR PA MANG ZHING GZHAN GYIS BSLU BA DANG 'KHOR MI 'DUM ZHING NGAN PA DANG YID DU MI 'ONG BA THOS SHING 'THAB MO'I TSIG TU 'GYUR BA DANG TSIG MI BTZUN PA'AM TSIG BZUNG MI 'OS SHING MA NGES PA'I SPOBS PAR 'GYUR BA DANG , 'DOD PA CHE ZHING CHO GA MI SHES PA DANG MI PHAN PA TSOL BA'AM PHAN PA MI TSOL BA DANG GZHAN LA GNOD PA BYED PA'AM GZHAN GYIS GNOD PA BYED PAR 'GYUR BA DANG LTA BA NGAN ZHING G-YO SGYU CAN DU 'GYUR BAR GSUNGS SO,",
        "wylie": "bden pa po'i le'u dang sa bcu pa'i mdo las ni de re re la 'bras bu gnyis gnyis gsungs te, gal te mir skyes na yang tshe thung la nad mang ba dang longs spyod chung la longs spyod gzhan dang thun mong ba dang g-yog 'khor mi bsrun pa'am yid brtan du mi rung la chung ma 'gran zla dang bcas pa dang , skur pa mang zhing gzhan gyis bslu ba dang 'khor mi 'dum zhing ngan pa dang yid du mi 'ong ba thos shing 'thab mo'i tshig tu 'gyur ba dang tshig mi btsun pa'am tshig bzung mi 'os shing ma nges pa'i spobs par 'gyur ba dang , 'dod pa che zhing cho ga mi shes pa dang mi phan pa tshol ba'am phan pa mi tshol ba dang gzhan la gnod pa byed pa'am gzhan gyis gnod pa byed par 'gyur ba dang lta ba ngan zhing g-yo sgyu can du 'gyur bar gsungs so",
        "english": "The Chapter on the True and the Sutra on the Ten Levels state that there are two such consequences for each of the ones given here; even if you do manage to take birth as a human, 1) Your life is short, and you get sick easily. 2) You don't have enough to live on, and what you do have is all just common property with others. 3) The people who work around you are \"inconsistent,\" which here means unreliable, and you find yourself having a lot of competition for your partner. 4) No one believes what you say, even when you are speaking the truth, and others are always deceiving you. 5) The people around you are always fighting against one another, and have an undesirable character. 6) You hear many unpleasant things, and when others talk to you it always seems to you as if they want to start a fight. 7) No one respects what you say--no one thinks that what you say has any particular value, and you are afflicted with a lack of confidence. 8) Your personality is dominated by desire, and you are never satisfied with what you have. 9) You are always finding yourself without help, or never find the help you need; and you are always hurting others, or always being hurt by others. 10) You become a person who keeps harmful views, or a deceitful person.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"C09\", \"acip\": \",BDEN PA PO'I LE'U DANG SA BCU PA'I MDO LAS NI DE RE RE LA 'BRAS BU GNYIS GNYIS GSUNGS TE, GAL TE MIR SKYES NA YANG TSE THUNG LA NAD MANG BA DANG LONGS SPYOD CHUNG LA LONGS SPYOD GZHAN DANG THUN MONG BA DANG G-YOG 'KHOR MI BSRUN PA'AM YID BRTAN DU MI RUNG LA CHUNG MA 'GRAN ZLA DANG BCAS PA DANG , SKUR PA MANG ZHING GZHAN GYIS BSLU BA DANG 'KHOR MI 'DUM ZHING NGAN PA DANG YID DU MI 'ONG BA THOS SHING 'THAB MO'I TSIG TU 'GYUR BA DANG TSIG MI BTZUN PA'AM TSIG BZUNG MI 'OS SHING MA NGES PA'I SPOBS PAR 'GYUR BA DANG , 'DOD PA CHE ZHING CHO GA MI SHES PA DANG MI PHAN PA TSOL BA'AM PHAN PA MI TSOL BA DANG GZHAN LA GNOD PA BYED PA'AM GZHAN GYIS GNOD PA BYED PAR 'GYUR BA DANG LTA BA NGAN ZHING G-YO SGYU CAN DU 'GYUR BAR GSUNGS SO,\", \"wylie\": \"bden pa po'i le'u dang sa bcu pa'i mdo las ni de re re la 'bras bu gnyis gnyis gsungs te, gal te mir skyes na yang tshe thung la nad mang ba dang longs spyod chung la longs spyod gzhan dang thun mong ba dang g-yog 'khor mi bsrun pa'am yid brtan du mi rung la chung ma 'gran zla dang bcas pa dang , skur pa mang zhing gzhan gyis bslu ba dang 'khor mi 'dum zhing ngan pa dang yid du mi 'ong ba thos shing 'thab mo'i tshig tu 'gyur ba dang tshig mi btsun pa'am tshig bzung mi 'os shing ma nges pa'i spobs par 'gyur ba dang , 'dod pa che zhing cho ga mi shes pa dang mi phan pa tshol ba'am phan pa mi tshol ba dang gzhan la gnod pa byed pa'am gzhan gyis gnod pa byed par 'gyur ba dang lta ba ngan zhing g-yo sgyu can du 'gyur bar gsungs so\", \"english\": \"The Chapter on the True and the Sutra on the Ten Levels state that there are two such consequences for each of the ones given here; even if you do manage to take birth as a human, 1) Your life is short, and you get sick easily. 2) You don't have enough to live on, and what you do have is all just common property with others. 3) The people who work around you are \\\"inconsistent,\\\" which here means unreliable, and you find yourself having a lot of competition for your partner. 4) No one believes what you say, even when you are speaking the truth, and others are always deceiving you. 5) The people around you are always fighting against one another, and have an undesirable character. 6) You hear many unpleasant things, and when others talk to you it always seems to you as if they want to start a fight. 7) No one respects what you say--no one thinks that what you say has any particular value, and you are afflicted with a lack of confidence. 8) Your personality is dominated by desire, and you are never satisfied with what you have. 9) You are always finding yourself without help, or never find the help you need; and you are always hurting others, or always being hurt by others. 10) You become a person who keeps harmful views, or a deceitful person.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 6159,
        "course": "C16",
        "seq": 141,
        "acip": "DE YANG BTANG SNYOMS SGOM PA LA THOG MAR DGRA GNYEN GANG YANG MA YIN PA'I BAR MA'I SEMS CAN ZHIG LA CHAGS SDANG GI SEMS SNYOMS, DE NAS RANG GI YID LA 'BAB PA'I GNYEN ZHIG DANG , YID DU MI 'ONG BA'I DGRA GNYIS MDUN DU BSAM STE, GNYEN 'DIS KYANG TSE RABS MANG POR DGRAR SKYES TE GNOD PA BYAS, DGRA 'DIS KYANG TSE RABS MANG POR GNYEN DU GYUR NAS PHAN BTAGS TSUL BSAM STE CHAGS SDANG GI SEMS SNYOMS,",
        "wylie": "de yang btang snyoms sgom pa la thog mar dgra gnyen gang yang ma yin pa'i bar ma'i sems can zhig la chags sdang gi sems snyoms, de nas rang gi yid la 'bab pa'i gnyen zhig dang , yid du mi 'ong ba'i dgra gnyis mdun du bsam ste, gnyen 'dis kyang tshe rabs mang por dgrar skyes te gnod pa byas, dgra 'dis kyang tshe rabs mang por gnyen du gyur nas phan btags tshul bsam ste chags sdang gi sems snyoms",
        "english": "The meditation on neutrality goes like this. First you put your thoughts in an even state, free of feelings of like and dislike, by thinking about someone who is for you a neutral figure: neither your enemy nor your friend. Then you imagine that two people are sitting before you: one of your best-loved friends, and one of your ugliest enemies. Next you think very carefully about how the friend has, in many of your previous lives, taken birth as your enemy and hurt you. You think too about how the enemy has, in so many of your past lives, taken birth as your friend and helped you. This puts your mind in the even state, free of feelings of like and dislike.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"C16\", \"acip\": \"DE YANG BTANG SNYOMS SGOM PA LA THOG MAR DGRA GNYEN GANG YANG MA YIN PA'I BAR MA'I SEMS CAN ZHIG LA CHAGS SDANG GI SEMS SNYOMS, DE NAS RANG GI YID LA 'BAB PA'I GNYEN ZHIG DANG , YID DU MI 'ONG BA'I DGRA GNYIS MDUN DU BSAM STE, GNYEN 'DIS KYANG TSE RABS MANG POR DGRAR SKYES TE GNOD PA BYAS, DGRA 'DIS KYANG TSE RABS MANG POR GNYEN DU GYUR NAS PHAN BTAGS TSUL BSAM STE CHAGS SDANG GI SEMS SNYOMS,\", \"wylie\": \"de yang btang snyoms sgom pa la thog mar dgra gnyen gang yang ma yin pa'i bar ma'i sems can zhig la chags sdang gi sems snyoms, de nas rang gi yid la 'bab pa'i gnyen zhig dang , yid du mi 'ong ba'i dgra gnyis mdun du bsam ste, gnyen 'dis kyang tshe rabs mang por dgrar skyes te gnod pa byas, dgra 'dis kyang tshe rabs mang por gnyen du gyur nas phan btags tshul bsam ste chags sdang gi sems snyoms\", \"english\": \"The meditation on neutrality goes like this. First you put your thoughts in an even state, free of feelings of like and dislike, by thinking about someone who is for you a neutral figure: neither your enemy nor your friend. Then you imagine that two people are sitting before you: one of your best-loved friends, and one of your ugliest enemies. Next you think very carefully about how the friend has, in many of your previous lives, taken birth as your enemy and hurt you. You think too about how the enemy has, in so many of your past lives, taken birth as your friend and helped you. This puts your mind in the even state, free of feelings of like and dislike.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 6762,
        "course": "C16",
        "seq": 744,
        "acip": "MDO LAS LAS DGE MI DGE LUNG MA BSTAN GSUM GSUNGS PA LAS DUS RE ZHIG LAS KYI RNAM SMIN YID DU 'ONG BA BDE BA MYONG BA DANG GTAN DU SDUG BSNGAL LAS SKYOB PA MYANG 'DAS THOB BYED NI DGE BA DANG , RNAM SMIN YID DU MI 'ONG BA MI BDE BA MYONG BA NI MI DGE BA DANG , YID DU 'ONG MI 'ONG SKYED PA DE GNYIS LAS GZHAN PA'I LAS NI DGE MI DGE LAS GZHAN PA LUNG MA BSTAN YIN NO,",
        "wylie": "mdo las las dge mi dge lung ma bstan gsum gsungs pa las dus re zhig las kyi rnam smin yid du 'ong ba bde ba myong ba dang gtan du sdug bsngal las skyob pa myang 'das thob byed ni dge ba dang , rnam smin yid du mi 'ong ba mi bde ba myong ba ni mi dge ba dang , yid du 'ong mi 'ong skyed pa de gnyis las gzhan pa'i las ni dge mi dge las gzhan pa lung ma bstan yin no",
        "english": "Sutra describes three kinds of karma: virtuous karma, non- virtuous karma, and neutral karma. Virtue is that karma which, in the short term, brings you a karmic ripening which is desirable (that is, a feeling of pleasure), and ultimately protects you from suffering (that is, helps you achieve nirvana). Non-virtue is that karma which brings you a karmic ripening which is undesirable (that is, a feeling of pain). A neutral deed, something neither virtuous nor non-virtuous, is that karma which brings you something which is neither desirable nor undesirable. We return next to the commentary of His Holiness the First Dalai Lama: 16 Deeds according to Result",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"C16\", \"acip\": \"MDO LAS LAS DGE MI DGE LUNG MA BSTAN GSUM GSUNGS PA LAS DUS RE ZHIG LAS KYI RNAM SMIN YID DU 'ONG BA BDE BA MYONG BA DANG GTAN DU SDUG BSNGAL LAS SKYOB PA MYANG 'DAS THOB BYED NI DGE BA DANG , RNAM SMIN YID DU MI 'ONG BA MI BDE BA MYONG BA NI MI DGE BA DANG , YID DU 'ONG MI 'ONG SKYED PA DE GNYIS LAS GZHAN PA'I LAS NI DGE MI DGE LAS GZHAN PA LUNG MA BSTAN YIN NO,\", \"wylie\": \"mdo las las dge mi dge lung ma bstan gsum gsungs pa las dus re zhig las kyi rnam smin yid du 'ong ba bde ba myong ba dang gtan du sdug bsngal las skyob pa myang 'das thob byed ni dge ba dang , rnam smin yid du mi 'ong ba mi bde ba myong ba ni mi dge ba dang , yid du 'ong mi 'ong skyed pa de gnyis las gzhan pa'i las ni dge mi dge las gzhan pa lung ma bstan yin no\", \"english\": \"Sutra describes three kinds of karma: virtuous karma, non- virtuous karma, and neutral karma. Virtue is that karma which, in the short term, brings you a karmic ripening which is desirable (that is, a feeling of pleasure), and ultimately protects you from suffering (that is, helps you achieve nirvana). Non-virtue is that karma which brings you a karmic ripening which is undesirable (that is, a feeling of pain). A neutral deed, something neither virtuous nor non-virtuous, is that karma which brings you something which is neither desirable nor undesirable. We return next to the commentary of His Holiness the First Dalai Lama: 16 Deeds according to Result\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 6790,
        "course": "C16",
        "seq": 772,
        "acip": ",RGYU MTHUN PA'I 'BRAS BU NI, NGAN 'GRO NAS MIR SKYES KYANG RIM PA LTAR TSE THUNG BA DANG LONGS SPYOD KYIS PHONGS PA DANG CHUNG MA MA BSRUNGS PAR 'GYUR BA DANG , SKUR PA MANG BA DANG MDZA' BO DANG 'BYE BA DANG YID DU MI 'ONG BA'I SGRA THOS PA DANG GZHAN GYIS TSIG MI NYAN PA DANG , CHAGS SDANG RMONGS GSUM SHAS CHE BA'O,",
        "wylie": "rgyu mthun pa'i 'bras bu ni, ngan 'gro nas mir skyes kyang rim pa ltar tshe thung ba dang longs spyod kyis phongs pa dang chung ma ma bsrungs par 'gyur ba dang , skur pa mang ba dang mdza' bo dang 'bye ba dang yid du mi 'ong ba'i sgra thos pa dang gzhan gyis tshig mi nyan pa dang , chags sdang rmongs gsum shas che ba'o",
        "english": "The \"consistent\" consequences are as follows. Even if you do manage to escape the realms of misery and take birth as a human, the following respective results occur to you: 1) Your life is short. 2) You don't have enough to live on. 3) You have problems keeping your partner from others. 4) People don't believe what you say, even when you're telling the truth. 5) You lose friends easily. 6) You hear things as bad sounds. 7) No one listens to you. 8) Your personality is dominated by desire. 9) Your personality is dominated by anger. 10) Your personality is dominated by stupidity.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"C16\", \"acip\": \",RGYU MTHUN PA'I 'BRAS BU NI, NGAN 'GRO NAS MIR SKYES KYANG RIM PA LTAR TSE THUNG BA DANG LONGS SPYOD KYIS PHONGS PA DANG CHUNG MA MA BSRUNGS PAR 'GYUR BA DANG , SKUR PA MANG BA DANG MDZA' BO DANG 'BYE BA DANG YID DU MI 'ONG BA'I SGRA THOS PA DANG GZHAN GYIS TSIG MI NYAN PA DANG , CHAGS SDANG RMONGS GSUM SHAS CHE BA'O,\", \"wylie\": \"rgyu mthun pa'i 'bras bu ni, ngan 'gro nas mir skyes kyang rim pa ltar tshe thung ba dang longs spyod kyis phongs pa dang chung ma ma bsrungs par 'gyur ba dang , skur pa mang ba dang mdza' bo dang 'bye ba dang yid du mi 'ong ba'i sgra thos pa dang gzhan gyis tshig mi nyan pa dang , chags sdang rmongs gsum shas che ba'o\", \"english\": \"The \\\"consistent\\\" consequences are as follows. Even if you do manage to escape the realms of misery and take birth as a human, the following respective results occur to you: 1) Your life is short. 2) You don't have enough to live on. 3) You have problems keeping your partner from others. 4) People don't believe what you say, even when you're telling the truth. 5) You lose friends easily. 6) You hear things as bad sounds. 7) No one listens to you. 8) Your personality is dominated by desire. 9) Your personality is dominated by anger. 10) Your personality is dominated by stupidity.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 6791,
        "course": "C16",
        "seq": 773,
        "acip": ",BDEN PA PO'I LE'U DANG SA BCU PA'I MDO LAS NI DE RE RE LA 'BRAS BU GNYIS GNYIS GSUNGS TE, GAL TE MIR SKYES NA YANG TSE THUNG LA NAD MANG BA DANG LONGS SPYOD CHUNG LA LONGS SPYOD GZHAN DANG THUN MONG BA DANG G-YOG 'KHOR MI BSRUN PA'AM YID BRTAN DU MI RUNG LA CHUNG MA 'GRAN ZLA DANG BCAS PA DANG , SKUR PA MANG ZHING GZHAN GYIS BSLU BA DANG 'KHOR MI 'DUM ZHING NGAN PA DANG YID DU MI 'ONG BA THOS SHING 'THAB MO'I TSIG TU 'GYUR BA DANG TSIG MI BTZUN PA'AM TSIG BZUNG MI 'OS SHING MA NGES PA'I SPOBS PAR 'GYUR BA DANG , 'DOD PA CHE ZHING CHOG MI SHES PA DANG MI PHAN PA TSOL BA'AM PHAN PA MI TSOL BA DANG GZHAN LA GNOD PA BYED PA'AM GZHAN GYIS GNOD PA BYED PAR 'GYUR BA DANG LTA BA NGAN ZHING G-YO SGYU CAN DU 'GYUR BAR GSUNGS SO,",
        "wylie": "bden pa po'i le'u dang sa bcu pa'i mdo las ni de re re la 'bras bu gnyis gnyis gsungs te, gal te mir skyes na yang tshe thung la nad mang ba dang longs spyod chung la longs spyod gzhan dang thun mong ba dang g-yog 'khor mi bsrun pa'am yid brtan du mi rung la chung ma 'gran zla dang bcas pa dang , skur pa mang zhing gzhan gyis bslu ba dang 'khor mi 'dum zhing ngan pa dang yid du mi 'ong ba thos shing 'thab mo'i tshig tu 'gyur ba dang tshig mi btsun pa'am tshig bzung mi 'os shing ma nges pa'i spobs par 'gyur ba dang , 'dod pa che zhing chog mi shes pa dang mi phan pa tshol ba'am phan pa mi tshol ba dang gzhan la gnod pa byed pa'am gzhan gyis gnod pa byed par 'gyur ba dang lta ba ngan zhing g-yo sgyu can du 'gyur bar gsungs so",
        "english": "The Chapter on the True and the Sutra on the Ten Levels state that there are two such consequences for each of the ones given here; even if you do manage to take birth as a human, 1) Your life is short, and you get sick easily. 2) You don't have enough to live on, and what you do have is all just common property with others. 3) The people who work around you are \"inconsistent,\" which here means unreliable, and you find yourself having a lot of competition for your partner. 4) No one believes what you say, even when you are speaking the truth, and others are always deceiving you. 5) The people around you are always fighting against one another, and have an undesirable character. 6) You hear many unpleasant things, and when others talk to you it always seems to you as if they want to start a fight. 7) No one respects what you say--no one thinks that what you say has any particular value, and you are afflicted with a lack of confidence. 8) Your personality is dominated by desire, and you are never satisfied with what you have. 9) You are always finding yourself without help, or never find the help you need; and you are always hurting others, or always being hurt by others. 10) You become a person who keeps harmful views, or a deceitful person.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"C16\", \"acip\": \",BDEN PA PO'I LE'U DANG SA BCU PA'I MDO LAS NI DE RE RE LA 'BRAS BU GNYIS GNYIS GSUNGS TE, GAL TE MIR SKYES NA YANG TSE THUNG LA NAD MANG BA DANG LONGS SPYOD CHUNG LA LONGS SPYOD GZHAN DANG THUN MONG BA DANG G-YOG 'KHOR MI BSRUN PA'AM YID BRTAN DU MI RUNG LA CHUNG MA 'GRAN ZLA DANG BCAS PA DANG , SKUR PA MANG ZHING GZHAN GYIS BSLU BA DANG 'KHOR MI 'DUM ZHING NGAN PA DANG YID DU MI 'ONG BA THOS SHING 'THAB MO'I TSIG TU 'GYUR BA DANG TSIG MI BTZUN PA'AM TSIG BZUNG MI 'OS SHING MA NGES PA'I SPOBS PAR 'GYUR BA DANG , 'DOD PA CHE ZHING CHOG MI SHES PA DANG MI PHAN PA TSOL BA'AM PHAN PA MI TSOL BA DANG GZHAN LA GNOD PA BYED PA'AM GZHAN GYIS GNOD PA BYED PAR 'GYUR BA DANG LTA BA NGAN ZHING G-YO SGYU CAN DU 'GYUR BAR GSUNGS SO,\", \"wylie\": \"bden pa po'i le'u dang sa bcu pa'i mdo las ni de re re la 'bras bu gnyis gnyis gsungs te, gal te mir skyes na yang tshe thung la nad mang ba dang longs spyod chung la longs spyod gzhan dang thun mong ba dang g-yog 'khor mi bsrun pa'am yid brtan du mi rung la chung ma 'gran zla dang bcas pa dang , skur pa mang zhing gzhan gyis bslu ba dang 'khor mi 'dum zhing ngan pa dang yid du mi 'ong ba thos shing 'thab mo'i tshig tu 'gyur ba dang tshig mi btsun pa'am tshig bzung mi 'os shing ma nges pa'i spobs par 'gyur ba dang , 'dod pa che zhing chog mi shes pa dang mi phan pa tshol ba'am phan pa mi tshol ba dang gzhan la gnod pa byed pa'am gzhan gyis gnod pa byed par 'gyur ba dang lta ba ngan zhing g-yo sgyu can du 'gyur bar gsungs so\", \"english\": \"The Chapter on the True and the Sutra on the Ten Levels state that there are two such consequences for each of the ones given here; even if you do manage to take birth as a human, 1) Your life is short, and you get sick easily. 2) You don't have enough to live on, and what you do have is all just common property with others. 3) The people who work around you are \\\"inconsistent,\\\" which here means unreliable, and you find yourself having a lot of competition for your partner. 4) No one believes what you say, even when you are speaking the truth, and others are always deceiving you. 5) The people around you are always fighting against one another, and have an undesirable character. 6) You hear many unpleasant things, and when others talk to you it always seems to you as if they want to start a fight. 7) No one respects what you say--no one thinks that what you say has any particular value, and you are afflicted with a lack of confidence. 8) Your personality is dominated by desire, and you are never satisfied with what you have. 9) You are always finding yourself without help, or never find the help you need; and you are always hurting others, or always being hurt by others. 10) You become a person who keeps harmful views, or a deceitful person.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 7450,
        "course": "C17",
        "seq": 412,
        "acip": ",DE LAS KYANG LUS DANG NGAG DANG YID KYI NYES SPYOD BCU DANG MTSAMS MED PA DANG DE DANG NYE BA DANG DAM PA'I CHOS SPONG BA LA SOGS PA MI DGE BA'I LAS NGAN 'GRO LA SOGS PA'I SDUG BSNGAL DRAG PO 'DREN PAR BYED PA LA MTHU PHUL DU BYUNG BA RNAMS NYI MA RE RE BZHIN JE RGYAS SU 'GRO LA, DE DAG GI GNYEN PO LEGS PAR GSUNGS PA'I CHOS KYI BDUD RTZI LA RGYAB KYIS JE PHYOGS SU SONG NAS MNGON MTHO DANG NGES LEGS KYI SROG BCAD DE, NGAN 'GRO SDUG BSNGAL DRAG CING RTZUB LA TSA ZHING YID DU MI 'ONG BA'I GNAS SU, 'CHI BAS NYE BAR BCOM NAS LAS NGAN PAS 'KHRID PAR BYED PAS NA DE LAS MA RUNGS PA'I SGO GZHAN CI ZHIG YOD,",
        "wylie": "de las kyang lus dang ngag dang yid kyi nyes spyod bcu dang mtshams med pa dang de dang nye ba dang dam pa'i chos spong ba la sogs pa mi dge ba'i las ngan 'gro la sogs pa'i sdug bsngal drag po 'dren par byed pa la mthu phul du byung ba rnams nyi ma re re bzhin je rgyas su 'gro la, de dag gi gnyen po legs par gsungs pa'i chos kyi bdud rtsi la rgyab kyis je phyogs su song nas mngon mtho dang nges legs kyi srog bcad de, ngan 'gro sdug bsngal drag cing rtsub la tsha zhing yid du mi 'ong ba'i gnas su, 'chi bas nye bar bcom nas las ngan pas 'khrid par byed pas na de las ma rungs pa'i sgo gzhan ci zhig yod",
        "english": "These afflictions in turn lead you to harmful deeds done in your acts, your words, and your thoughts: deeds like the ten non-virtues, and the five \"immediate\" deeds, and the five that are close to these, and giving up the highest Dharma, and on and on. Every single day then deeds like these, of tremendous power, capable of leading you to the sufferings of the three lower realms and the like, will tend to increase, further and further. The antidote for all these deeds is the nectar of the Dharma, spoken so true, and the further you turn from it then the more tightly you strangle your chances for the higher realms, and ultimate good. Death will rip away your life, and the wrong deeds you have done will drag you to the lower realms, to a fearful place of mighty and savage suffering, to the fires. And so I ask you, where could you find any thought more disastrous for you than this idea, that what is impermanent could be permanent? 28 The Benefits of Meditating on Death",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"C17\", \"acip\": \",DE LAS KYANG LUS DANG NGAG DANG YID KYI NYES SPYOD BCU DANG MTSAMS MED PA DANG DE DANG NYE BA DANG DAM PA'I CHOS SPONG BA LA SOGS PA MI DGE BA'I LAS NGAN 'GRO LA SOGS PA'I SDUG BSNGAL DRAG PO 'DREN PAR BYED PA LA MTHU PHUL DU BYUNG BA RNAMS NYI MA RE RE BZHIN JE RGYAS SU 'GRO LA, DE DAG GI GNYEN PO LEGS PAR GSUNGS PA'I CHOS KYI BDUD RTZI LA RGYAB KYIS JE PHYOGS SU SONG NAS MNGON MTHO DANG NGES LEGS KYI SROG BCAD DE, NGAN 'GRO SDUG BSNGAL DRAG CING RTZUB LA TSA ZHING YID DU MI 'ONG BA'I GNAS SU, 'CHI BAS NYE BAR BCOM NAS LAS NGAN PAS 'KHRID PAR BYED PAS NA DE LAS MA RUNGS PA'I SGO GZHAN CI ZHIG YOD,\", \"wylie\": \"de las kyang lus dang ngag dang yid kyi nyes spyod bcu dang mtshams med pa dang de dang nye ba dang dam pa'i chos spong ba la sogs pa mi dge ba'i las ngan 'gro la sogs pa'i sdug bsngal drag po 'dren par byed pa la mthu phul du byung ba rnams nyi ma re re bzhin je rgyas su 'gro la, de dag gi gnyen po legs par gsungs pa'i chos kyi bdud rtsi la rgyab kyis je phyogs su song nas mngon mtho dang nges legs kyi srog bcad de, ngan 'gro sdug bsngal drag cing rtsub la tsha zhing yid du mi 'ong ba'i gnas su, 'chi bas nye bar bcom nas las ngan pas 'khrid par byed pas na de las ma rungs pa'i sgo gzhan ci zhig yod\", \"english\": \"These afflictions in turn lead you to harmful deeds done in your acts, your words, and your thoughts: deeds like the ten non-virtues, and the five \\\"immediate\\\" deeds, and the five that are close to these, and giving up the highest Dharma, and on and on. Every single day then deeds like these, of tremendous power, capable of leading you to the sufferings of the three lower realms and the like, will tend to increase, further and further. The antidote for all these deeds is the nectar of the Dharma, spoken so true, and the further you turn from it then the more tightly you strangle your chances for the higher realms, and ultimate good. Death will rip away your life, and the wrong deeds you have done will drag you to the lower realms, to a fearful place of mighty and savage suffering, to the fires. And so I ask you, where could you find any thought more disastrous for you than this idea, that what is impermanent could be permanent? 28 The Benefits of Meditating on Death\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 7536,
        "course": "C17",
        "seq": 498,
        "acip": ",RGYU MTHUN PA'I 'BRAS BU NI, NGAN 'GRO NAS MIR SKYES KYANG RIM PA LTAR TSE THUNG BA DANG LONGS SPYOD KYIS PHONGS PA DANG CHUNG MA MA BSRUNGS PAR 'GYUR BA DANG , SKUR PA MANG BA DANG MDZA' BO DANG 'BYE BA DANG YID DU MI 'ONG BA'I SGRA THOS PA DANG GZHAN GYIS TSIG MI NYAN PA DANG , CHAGS SDANG RMONGS GSUM SHAS CHE BA'O,",
        "wylie": "rgyu mthun pa'i 'bras bu ni, ngan 'gro nas mir skyes kyang rim pa ltar tshe thung ba dang longs spyod kyis phongs pa dang chung ma ma bsrungs par 'gyur ba dang , skur pa mang ba dang mdza' bo dang 'bye ba dang yid du mi 'ong ba'i sgra thos pa dang gzhan gyis tshig mi nyan pa dang , chags sdang rmongs gsum shas che ba'o",
        "english": "The \"consistent\" consequences are as follows. Even if you do manage to escape the realms of misery and take birth as a human, the following respective results occur to you: 1) Your life is short. 2) You don't have enough to live on. 3) You have problems keeping your partner from others. 4) People don't believe what you say, even when you're telling the truth. 5) You lose friends easily. 6) You hear things as bad sounds. 7) No one listens to you. 8) Your personality is dominated by desire. 9) Your personality is dominated by anger. 10) Your personality is dominated by stupidity.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"C17\", \"acip\": \",RGYU MTHUN PA'I 'BRAS BU NI, NGAN 'GRO NAS MIR SKYES KYANG RIM PA LTAR TSE THUNG BA DANG LONGS SPYOD KYIS PHONGS PA DANG CHUNG MA MA BSRUNGS PAR 'GYUR BA DANG , SKUR PA MANG BA DANG MDZA' BO DANG 'BYE BA DANG YID DU MI 'ONG BA'I SGRA THOS PA DANG GZHAN GYIS TSIG MI NYAN PA DANG , CHAGS SDANG RMONGS GSUM SHAS CHE BA'O,\", \"wylie\": \"rgyu mthun pa'i 'bras bu ni, ngan 'gro nas mir skyes kyang rim pa ltar tshe thung ba dang longs spyod kyis phongs pa dang chung ma ma bsrungs par 'gyur ba dang , skur pa mang ba dang mdza' bo dang 'bye ba dang yid du mi 'ong ba'i sgra thos pa dang gzhan gyis tshig mi nyan pa dang , chags sdang rmongs gsum shas che ba'o\", \"english\": \"The \\\"consistent\\\" consequences are as follows. Even if you do manage to escape the realms of misery and take birth as a human, the following respective results occur to you: 1) Your life is short. 2) You don't have enough to live on. 3) You have problems keeping your partner from others. 4) People don't believe what you say, even when you're telling the truth. 5) You lose friends easily. 6) You hear things as bad sounds. 7) No one listens to you. 8) Your personality is dominated by desire. 9) Your personality is dominated by anger. 10) Your personality is dominated by stupidity.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 7537,
        "course": "C17",
        "seq": 499,
        "acip": ",BDEN PA PO'I LE'U DANG SA BCU PA'I MDO LAS NI DE RE RE LA 'BRAS BU GNYIS GNYIS GSUNGS TE, GAL TE MIR SKYES NA YANG TSE THUNG LA NAD MANG BA DANG LONGS SPYOD CHUNG LA LONGS SPYOD GZHAN DANG THUN MONG BA DANG G-YOG 'KHOR MI BSRUN PA'AM YID BRTAN DU MI RUNG LA CHUNG MA 'GRAN ZLA DANG BCAS PA DANG , SKUR PA MANG ZHING GZHAN GYIS BSLU BA DANG 'KHOR MI 'DUM ZHING NGAN PA DANG YID DU MI 'ONG BA THOS SHING 'THAB MO'I TSIG TU 'GYUR BA DANG TSIG MI BTZUN PA'AM TSIG BZUNG MI 'OS SHING MA NGES PA'I SPOBS PAR 'GYUR BA DANG , 'DOD PA CHE ZHING CHO GA MI SHES PA DANG MI PHAN PA TSOL BA'AM PHAN PA MI TSOL BA DANG GZHAN LA GNOD PA BYED PA'AM GZHAN GYIS GNOD PA BYED PAR 'GYUR BA DANG LTA BA NGAN ZHING G-YO SGYU CAN DU 'GYUR BAR GSUNGS SO,",
        "wylie": "bden pa po'i le'u dang sa bcu pa'i mdo las ni de re re la 'bras bu gnyis gnyis gsungs te, gal te mir skyes na yang tshe thung la nad mang ba dang longs spyod chung la longs spyod gzhan dang thun mong ba dang g-yog 'khor mi bsrun pa'am yid brtan du mi rung la chung ma 'gran zla dang bcas pa dang , skur pa mang zhing gzhan gyis bslu ba dang 'khor mi 'dum zhing ngan pa dang yid du mi 'ong ba thos shing 'thab mo'i tshig tu 'gyur ba dang tshig mi btsun pa'am tshig bzung mi 'os shing ma nges pa'i spobs par 'gyur ba dang , 'dod pa che zhing cho ga mi shes pa dang mi phan pa tshol ba'am phan pa mi tshol ba dang gzhan la gnod pa byed pa'am gzhan gyis gnod pa byed par 'gyur ba dang lta ba ngan zhing g-yo sgyu can du 'gyur bar gsungs so",
        "english": "The Chapter on the True and the Sutra on the Ten Levels state that there are two such consequences for each of the ones given here; even if you do manage to take birth as a human, 1) Your life is short, and you get sick easily. 2) You don't have enough to live on, and what you do have is all just common property with others. 3) The people who work around you are \"inconsistent,\" which here means unreliable, and you find yourself having a lot of competition for your partner. 4) No one believes what you say, even when you are speaking the truth, and others are always deceiving you. 5) The people around you are always fighting against one another, and have an undesirable character. 6) You hear many unpleasant things, and when others talk to you it always seems to you as if they want to start a fight. 7) No one respects what you say--no one thinks that what you say has any particular value, and you are afflicted with a lack of confidence. 8) Your personality is dominated by desire, and you are never satisfied with what you have. 9) You are always finding yourself without help, or never find the help you need; and you are always hurting others, or always being hurt by others. 10) You become a person who keeps harmful views, or a deceitful person.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"C17\", \"acip\": \",BDEN PA PO'I LE'U DANG SA BCU PA'I MDO LAS NI DE RE RE LA 'BRAS BU GNYIS GNYIS GSUNGS TE, GAL TE MIR SKYES NA YANG TSE THUNG LA NAD MANG BA DANG LONGS SPYOD CHUNG LA LONGS SPYOD GZHAN DANG THUN MONG BA DANG G-YOG 'KHOR MI BSRUN PA'AM YID BRTAN DU MI RUNG LA CHUNG MA 'GRAN ZLA DANG BCAS PA DANG , SKUR PA MANG ZHING GZHAN GYIS BSLU BA DANG 'KHOR MI 'DUM ZHING NGAN PA DANG YID DU MI 'ONG BA THOS SHING 'THAB MO'I TSIG TU 'GYUR BA DANG TSIG MI BTZUN PA'AM TSIG BZUNG MI 'OS SHING MA NGES PA'I SPOBS PAR 'GYUR BA DANG , 'DOD PA CHE ZHING CHO GA MI SHES PA DANG MI PHAN PA TSOL BA'AM PHAN PA MI TSOL BA DANG GZHAN LA GNOD PA BYED PA'AM GZHAN GYIS GNOD PA BYED PAR 'GYUR BA DANG LTA BA NGAN ZHING G-YO SGYU CAN DU 'GYUR BAR GSUNGS SO,\", \"wylie\": \"bden pa po'i le'u dang sa bcu pa'i mdo las ni de re re la 'bras bu gnyis gnyis gsungs te, gal te mir skyes na yang tshe thung la nad mang ba dang longs spyod chung la longs spyod gzhan dang thun mong ba dang g-yog 'khor mi bsrun pa'am yid brtan du mi rung la chung ma 'gran zla dang bcas pa dang , skur pa mang zhing gzhan gyis bslu ba dang 'khor mi 'dum zhing ngan pa dang yid du mi 'ong ba thos shing 'thab mo'i tshig tu 'gyur ba dang tshig mi btsun pa'am tshig bzung mi 'os shing ma nges pa'i spobs par 'gyur ba dang , 'dod pa che zhing cho ga mi shes pa dang mi phan pa tshol ba'am phan pa mi tshol ba dang gzhan la gnod pa byed pa'am gzhan gyis gnod pa byed par 'gyur ba dang lta ba ngan zhing g-yo sgyu can du 'gyur bar gsungs so\", \"english\": \"The Chapter on the True and the Sutra on the Ten Levels state that there are two such consequences for each of the ones given here; even if you do manage to take birth as a human, 1) Your life is short, and you get sick easily. 2) You don't have enough to live on, and what you do have is all just common property with others. 3) The people who work around you are \\\"inconsistent,\\\" which here means unreliable, and you find yourself having a lot of competition for your partner. 4) No one believes what you say, even when you are speaking the truth, and others are always deceiving you. 5) The people around you are always fighting against one another, and have an undesirable character. 6) You hear many unpleasant things, and when others talk to you it always seems to you as if they want to start a fight. 7) No one respects what you say--no one thinks that what you say has any particular value, and you are afflicted with a lack of confidence. 8) Your personality is dominated by desire, and you are never satisfied with what you have. 9) You are always finding yourself without help, or never find the help you need; and you are always hurting others, or always being hurt by others. 10) You become a person who keeps harmful views, or a deceitful person.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 33711,
        "course": "EM",
        "seq": 1003,
        "acip": ",'PHRO BA DANG RGOD PA GNYIS LA KHYAD CHE STE, DGRA LTA BU YUL YID DU MI 'ONG BA LA MNAR SEMS PA'I SKABS KYI 'PHRO BA DANG, ZHI GNAS BSGOM PA'I TSE SBYIN PA TSUL KHRIMS SOGS DGE BA'I YUL LA 'PHRO BA LTA BU NI 'PHRO BA YIN YANG RGOD PA MIN NO,,",
        "wylie": "'phro ba dang rgod pa gnyis la khyad che ste, dgra lta bu yul yid du mi 'ong ba la mnar sems pa'i skabs kyi 'phro ba dang, zhi gnas bsgom pa'i tshe sbyin pa tshul khrims sogs dge ba'i yul la 'phro ba lta bu ni 'phro ba yin yang rgod pa min no",
        "english": "Now there's a big difference here between what we've called “the mind flying off to objects” and this phenomenon of mental agitation. Our mind can fly off to an object during a moment of sheer malice, and we start thinking about some unpleasant object such as a person we don't like. At the same time, the mind can also fly off to a virtuous object—such as an act of giving, or morality—inside of a meditation session as we try to reach quietude. We would call this “the mind flying off,” but we wouldn't call it “agitation.”",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"EM\", \"acip\": \",'PHRO BA DANG RGOD PA GNYIS LA KHYAD CHE STE, DGRA LTA BU YUL YID DU MI 'ONG BA LA MNAR SEMS PA'I SKABS KYI 'PHRO BA DANG, ZHI GNAS BSGOM PA'I TSE SBYIN PA TSUL KHRIMS SOGS DGE BA'I YUL LA 'PHRO BA LTA BU NI 'PHRO BA YIN YANG RGOD PA MIN NO,,\", \"wylie\": \"'phro ba dang rgod pa gnyis la khyad che ste, dgra lta bu yul yid du mi 'ong ba la mnar sems pa'i skabs kyi 'phro ba dang, zhi gnas bsgom pa'i tshe sbyin pa tshul khrims sogs dge ba'i yul la 'phro ba lta bu ni 'phro ba yin yang rgod pa min no\", \"english\": \"Now there's a big difference here between what we've called “the mind flying off to objects” and this phenomenon of mental agitation. Our mind can fly off to an object during a moment of sheer malice, and we start thinking about some unpleasant object such as a person we don't like. At the same time, the mind can also fly off to a virtuous object—such as an act of giving, or morality—inside of a meditation session as we try to reach quietude. We would call this “the mind flying off,” but we wouldn't call it “agitation.”\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 28068,
        "course": "ILL",
        "seq": 749,
        "acip": ",DE LTAR DGOS PA MED PAR MA ZAD 'JIG RTEN PHA ROL GYI DON DANG YANG NI 'GAL BAR 'GYUR TE, KHONG KHRO LA SKABS BYIN PAS SHI BA'I 'OG TU RNAM SMIN YID DU MI 'ONG BA 'PHEN PA'I PHYIR RO,,",
        "wylie": "de ltar dgos pa med par ma zad 'jig rten pha rol gyi don dang yang ni 'gal bar 'gyur te, khong khro la skabs byin pas shi ba'i 'og tu rnam smin yid du mi 'ong ba 'phen pa'i phyir ro",
        "english": "Not only is the anger thus pointless, but it also contradicts your goals for the world beyond; that is, if you allow yourself feelings of anger, then it will project ahead of you—after your death—an upleasant karmic ripening. Wishes for revenge & to avoid pain are contradictory",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"ILL\", \"acip\": \",DE LTAR DGOS PA MED PAR MA ZAD 'JIG RTEN PHA ROL GYI DON DANG YANG NI 'GAL BAR 'GYUR TE, KHONG KHRO LA SKABS BYIN PAS SHI BA'I 'OG TU RNAM SMIN YID DU MI 'ONG BA 'PHEN PA'I PHYIR RO,,\", \"wylie\": \"de ltar dgos pa med par ma zad 'jig rten pha rol gyi don dang yang ni 'gal bar 'gyur te, khong khro la skabs byin pas shi ba'i 'og tu rnam smin yid du mi 'ong ba 'phen pa'i phyir ro\", \"english\": \"Not only is the anger thus pointless, but it also contradicts your goals for the world beyond; that is, if you allow yourself feelings of anger, then it will project ahead of you—after your death—an upleasant karmic ripening. Wishes for revenge & to avoid pain are contradictory\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 28072,
        "course": "ILL",
        "seq": 753,
        "acip": "RANG GI LUS LA GNOD PA'I SDUG BSNGAL CHEN PO DGRA DAG GIS BSGRUBS PA DE NI, SNGON BYAS PA YI SROG GCOD KYI MI DGE BA'I LAS KYI 'BRAS BU, NGAN SONG GSUM DU RNAM SMIN DRAG PO MYONG ZHING, RGYU MTHUN GYI 'BRAS BU LHAG MAR LUS PA CAN RNAMS KYI, RGYU MTHUN GYI 'BRAS BU YID DU MI 'ONG BA MA LUS PA LDOG PA'I RGYU GANG YIN PA,",
        "wylie": "rang gi lus la gnod pa'i sdug bsngal chen po dgra dag gis bsgrubs pa de ni, sngon byas pa yi srog gcod kyi mi dge ba'i las kyi 'bras bu, ngan song gsum du rnam smin drag po myong zhing, rgyu mthun gyi 'bras bu lhag mar lus pa can rnams kyi, rgyu mthun gyi 'bras bu yid du mi 'ong ba ma lus pa ldog pa'i rgyu gang yin pa",
        "english": "And so now think about the great pain that people who hate you might be inflicting upon your body. This is the consequence of a negative deed that you've done in the past: the taking of life, and something which you would normally have to experience as a violent karmic ripening in one of the lower realms. It also serves to expiate all the rest of the remaining homogenous results—all the rest of the unpleasant homogenous results.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"ILL\", \"acip\": \"RANG GI LUS LA GNOD PA'I SDUG BSNGAL CHEN PO DGRA DAG GIS BSGRUBS PA DE NI, SNGON BYAS PA YI SROG GCOD KYI MI DGE BA'I LAS KYI 'BRAS BU, NGAN SONG GSUM DU RNAM SMIN DRAG PO MYONG ZHING, RGYU MTHUN GYI 'BRAS BU LHAG MAR LUS PA CAN RNAMS KYI, RGYU MTHUN GYI 'BRAS BU YID DU MI 'ONG BA MA LUS PA LDOG PA'I RGYU GANG YIN PA,\", \"wylie\": \"rang gi lus la gnod pa'i sdug bsngal chen po dgra dag gis bsgrubs pa de ni, sngon byas pa yi srog gcod kyi mi dge ba'i las kyi 'bras bu, ngan song gsum du rnam smin drag po myong zhing, rgyu mthun gyi 'bras bu lhag mar lus pa can rnams kyi, rgyu mthun gyi 'bras bu yid du mi 'ong ba ma lus pa ldog pa'i rgyu gang yin pa\", \"english\": \"And so now think about the great pain that people who hate you might be inflicting upon your body. This is the consequence of a negative deed that you've done in the past: the taking of life, and something which you would normally have to experience as a violent karmic ripening in one of the lower realms. It also serves to expiate all the rest of the remaining homogenous results—all the rest of the unpleasant homogenous results.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 28078,
        "course": "ILL",
        "seq": 759,
        "acip": "DANG PO NI, MI BZOD PA NI RNAM SMIN YID DU MI 'ONG BA YANGS PA 'PHEN PA'I RGYU YIN PA 'BA' ZHIG TU MA ZAD KYI, YUN RING DU BSAGS PA'I BSOD NAMS KYI TSOGS ZAD PA'I RGYU YANG YIN NO, ZHES STON PA NI,",
        "wylie": "dang po ni, mi bzod pa ni rnam smin yid du mi 'ong ba yangs pa 'phen pa'i rgyu yin pa 'ba' zhig tu ma zad kyi, yun ring du bsags pa'i bsod nams kyi tshogs zad pa'i rgyu yang yin no, zhes ston pa ni",
        "english": "Here is the first. The author next demonstrates how failing to maintain our patience not only acts as a cause which projects extensive, unpleasant karmic results; but at the same time serves as a cause which wears away the accumulation of good karma that has taken us a very long period of time to put together.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"ILL\", \"acip\": \"DANG PO NI, MI BZOD PA NI RNAM SMIN YID DU MI 'ONG BA YANGS PA 'PHEN PA'I RGYU YIN PA 'BA' ZHIG TU MA ZAD KYI, YUN RING DU BSAGS PA'I BSOD NAMS KYI TSOGS ZAD PA'I RGYU YANG YIN NO, ZHES STON PA NI,\", \"wylie\": \"dang po ni, mi bzod pa ni rnam smin yid du mi 'ong ba yangs pa 'phen pa'i rgyu yin pa 'ba' zhig tu ma zad kyi, yun ring du bsags pa'i bsod nams kyi tshogs zad pa'i rgyu yang yin no, zhes ston pa ni\", \"english\": \"Here is the first. The author next demonstrates how failing to maintain our patience not only acts as a cause which projects extensive, unpleasant karmic results; but at the same time serves as a cause which wears away the accumulation of good karma that has taken us a very long period of time to put together.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 28082,
        "course": "ILL",
        "seq": 763,
        "acip": "DE YI PHYIR DE LTAR NA 'BRAS BU YID DU MI 'ONG BA 'PHEN PA DANG, DGE BA LA GNOD PA BYED PA'I SDIG PA NI, MI BZOD PA KHONG KHRO LAS GZHAN PA'I MCHOG TU GYUR PA YOD PA MA YIN NO,,",
        "wylie": "de yi phyir de ltar na 'bras bu yid du mi 'ong ba 'phen pa dang, dge ba la gnod pa byed pa'i sdig pa ni, mi bzod pa khong khro las gzhan pa'i mchog tu gyur pa yod pa ma yin no",
        "english": "And thus—meaning “therefore”—there exists no negative deed which is more effective than anger, losing ones patience, for projecting unpleasant karmic consequences into the future, and for damaging ones good karma.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"ILL\", \"acip\": \"DE YI PHYIR DE LTAR NA 'BRAS BU YID DU MI 'ONG BA 'PHEN PA DANG, DGE BA LA GNOD PA BYED PA'I SDIG PA NI, MI BZOD PA KHONG KHRO LAS GZHAN PA'I MCHOG TU GYUR PA YOD PA MA YIN NO,,\", \"wylie\": \"de yi phyir de ltar na 'bras bu yid du mi 'ong ba 'phen pa dang, dge ba la gnod pa byed pa'i sdig pa ni, mi bzod pa khong khro las gzhan pa'i mchog tu gyur pa yod pa ma yin no\", \"english\": \"And thus—meaning “therefore”—there exists no negative deed which is more effective than anger, losing ones patience, for projecting unpleasant karmic consequences into the future, and for damaging ones good karma.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 29296,
        "course": "ILL",
        "seq": 1977,
        "acip": "RAB RIB CAN GYI MIG GIS SKRA SHAD SOGS MTHONG BA DANG, BONG BU'I RVA LA SOGS PA MI MTHONG BA'I NGES PA DE'I PHYIR RNAM SMIN YID DU 'ONG BA NI MI DGE BA LAS MI 'BYUNG LA, RNAM SMIN YID DU MI 'ONG BA NI DGE BA LAS MA YIN PA'I PHYIR, RNAM SMIN MI DGE BA STE YID DU MI 'ONG BA NI, NAG PO'I LAS LAS YIN LA, RNAM SMIN DGE BA STE YID DU 'ONG BA NI DGE BA LAS 'BYUNG BA YIN PAR MTHONG ZHING,",
        "wylie": "rab rib can gyi mig gis skra shad sogs mthong ba dang, bong bu'i rva la sogs pa mi mthong ba'i nges pa de'i phyir rnam smin yid du 'ong ba ni mi dge ba las mi 'byung la, rnam smin yid du mi 'ong ba ni dge ba las ma yin pa'i phyir, rnam smin mi dge ba ste yid du mi 'ong ba ni, nag po'i las las yin la, rnam smin dge ba ste yid du 'ong ba ni dge ba las 'byung ba yin par mthong zhing",
        "english": "Eyes affected by cataracts see things like strands of hair; but it is definite that they do not see things like horns on top of the head of a rabbit. As such, it is not the case that a pleasant ripening of karma can come from a non-virtuous deed; and neither can an unpleasant ripening come from a virtuous deed. We can see then that a non-virtuous ripening—an unpleasant one—is something that comes from a black karma; while a virtuous ripening—a pleasant one—is something that comes from a good deed.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"ILL\", \"acip\": \"RAB RIB CAN GYI MIG GIS SKRA SHAD SOGS MTHONG BA DANG, BONG BU'I RVA LA SOGS PA MI MTHONG BA'I NGES PA DE'I PHYIR RNAM SMIN YID DU 'ONG BA NI MI DGE BA LAS MI 'BYUNG LA, RNAM SMIN YID DU MI 'ONG BA NI DGE BA LAS MA YIN PA'I PHYIR, RNAM SMIN MI DGE BA STE YID DU MI 'ONG BA NI, NAG PO'I LAS LAS YIN LA, RNAM SMIN DGE BA STE YID DU 'ONG BA NI DGE BA LAS 'BYUNG BA YIN PAR MTHONG ZHING,\", \"wylie\": \"rab rib can gyi mig gis skra shad sogs mthong ba dang, bong bu'i rva la sogs pa mi mthong ba'i nges pa de'i phyir rnam smin yid du 'ong ba ni mi dge ba las mi 'byung la, rnam smin yid du mi 'ong ba ni dge ba las ma yin pa'i phyir, rnam smin mi dge ba ste yid du mi 'ong ba ni, nag po'i las las yin la, rnam smin dge ba ste yid du 'ong ba ni dge ba las 'byung ba yin par mthong zhing\", \"english\": \"Eyes affected by cataracts see things like strands of hair; but it is definite that they do not see things like horns on top of the head of a rabbit. As such, it is not the case that a pleasant ripening of karma can come from a non-virtuous deed; and neither can an unpleasant ripening come from a virtuous deed. We can see then that a non-virtuous ripening—an unpleasant one—is something that comes from a black karma; while a virtuous ripening—a pleasant one—is something that comes from a good deed.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 31632,
        "course": "ILL",
        "seq": 4313,
        "acip": "DPER NA MI DGE BA LAS RNAM SMIN YID DU MI 'ONG BA 'BYUNG BA DANG, 'PHAGS PA SLOB PA'I LAM LAS MYANG 'DAS 'THOB PA LA SOGS PA'O,,",
        "wylie": "dper na mi dge ba las rnam smin yid du mi 'ong ba 'byung ba dang, 'phags pa slob pa'i lam las myang 'das 'thob pa la sogs pa'o",
        "english": "It's like the examples of how unpleasant ripenings derive from non-virtue; or how realized beings attain nirvana from the paths of those who are still learning, and so on.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"ILL\", \"acip\": \"DPER NA MI DGE BA LAS RNAM SMIN YID DU MI 'ONG BA 'BYUNG BA DANG, 'PHAGS PA SLOB PA'I LAM LAS MYANG 'DAS 'THOB PA LA SOGS PA'O,,\", \"wylie\": \"dper na mi dge ba las rnam smin yid du mi 'ong ba 'byung ba dang, 'phags pa slob pa'i lam las myang 'das 'thob pa la sogs pa'o\", \"english\": \"It's like the examples of how unpleasant ripenings derive from non-virtue; or how realized beings attain nirvana from the paths of those who are still learning, and so on.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 31633,
        "course": "ILL",
        "seq": 4314,
        "acip": "DE LTAR BSHAD PA LAS BZLOG PA NI GNAS MIN PA ZHES BYA STE, DPER NA DGE BA LAS RNAM SMIN YID DU MI 'ONG BA 'BYUNG BA DANG, MTHONG LAM THOB PAS LAS DBANG GIS SRID PA BRGYAD PA 'GRUB PA NI GNAS MA YIN ZHING GO SKABS MED PA LTA BU'O,,",
        "wylie": "de ltar bshad pa las bzlog pa ni gnas min pa zhes bya ste, dper na dge ba las rnam smin yid du mi 'ong ba 'byung ba dang, mthong lam thob pas las dbang gis srid pa brgyad pa 'grub pa ni gnas ma yin zhing go skabs med pa lta bu'o",
        "english": "Anything that could happen in the opposite way from what we have described here then would be called what is “not actual.” For example, it would not be actual (there would be no chance of it) if a virtuous action led to an unpleasant ripening; or if an individual had attained the path of seeing and then—due to the power of karma—were to experience an eighth rebirth afterwards.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"ILL\", \"acip\": \"DE LTAR BSHAD PA LAS BZLOG PA NI GNAS MIN PA ZHES BYA STE, DPER NA DGE BA LAS RNAM SMIN YID DU MI 'ONG BA 'BYUNG BA DANG, MTHONG LAM THOB PAS LAS DBANG GIS SRID PA BRGYAD PA 'GRUB PA NI GNAS MA YIN ZHING GO SKABS MED PA LTA BU'O,,\", \"wylie\": \"de ltar bshad pa las bzlog pa ni gnas min pa zhes bya ste, dper na dge ba las rnam smin yid du mi 'ong ba 'byung ba dang, mthong lam thob pas las dbang gis srid pa brgyad pa 'grub pa ni gnas ma yin zhing go skabs med pa lta bu'o\", \"english\": \"Anything that could happen in the opposite way from what we have described here then would be called what is “not actual.” For example, it would not be actual (there would be no chance of it) if a virtuous action led to an unpleasant ripening; or if an individual had attained the path of seeing and then—due to the power of karma—were to experience an eighth rebirth afterwards.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 34588,
        "course": "P5",
        "seq": 11,
        "acip": "DE DAG GI GNYEN PO LEGS PAR GSUNGS PA'I, CHOS KYI BDUD RTZI LA RGYAB KYIS JE PHYOGS SU SONG NAS MNGON MTHO DANG NGES LEGS KYI SROG BCAD DE NGAN 'GRO SDUG BSNGAL DRAG CING RTZUB LA TSA ZHING YID DU MI 'ONG BA'I GNAS SU 'CHI BAS NYE BAR BCOM NAS LAS NGAN PAS 'KHRID PAR BYED PAS NA DE LAS MA RUNGS PA'I SGO GZHAN CI ZHIG YOD",
        "wylie": "de dag gi gnyen po legs par gsungs pa'i, chos kyi bdud rtsi la rgyab kyis je phyogs su song nas mngon mtho dang nges legs kyi srog bcad de ngan 'gro sdug bsngal drag cing rtsub la tsha zhing yid du mi 'ong ba'i gnas su 'chi bas nye bar bcom nas las ngan pas 'khrid par byed pas na de las ma rungs pa'i sgo gzhan ci zhig yod",
        "english": "The antidote for all these deeds is the nectar of the Dharma, spoken so true— and the further you turn from it then the more tightly you strangle your chances for the higher realms, and ultimate good. Death will rip away your life, and the wrongdeeds you have done will dragyou to the lower realms, to a fearful place of mighty and savage suffering, to the fires. And so I ask you, where could you find any thought more disastrous for you than this idea, that what is impermanent could ever be permanent?",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"P5\", \"acip\": \"DE DAG GI GNYEN PO LEGS PAR GSUNGS PA'I, CHOS KYI BDUD RTZI LA RGYAB KYIS JE PHYOGS SU SONG NAS MNGON MTHO DANG NGES LEGS KYI SROG BCAD DE NGAN 'GRO SDUG BSNGAL DRAG CING RTZUB LA TSA ZHING YID DU MI 'ONG BA'I GNAS SU 'CHI BAS NYE BAR BCOM NAS LAS NGAN PAS 'KHRID PAR BYED PAS NA DE LAS MA RUNGS PA'I SGO GZHAN CI ZHIG YOD\", \"wylie\": \"de dag gi gnyen po legs par gsungs pa'i, chos kyi bdud rtsi la rgyab kyis je phyogs su song nas mngon mtho dang nges legs kyi srog bcad de ngan 'gro sdug bsngal drag cing rtsub la tsha zhing yid du mi 'ong ba'i gnas su 'chi bas nye bar bcom nas las ngan pas 'khrid par byed pas na de las ma rungs pa'i sgo gzhan ci zhig yod\", \"english\": \"The antidote for all these deeds is the nectar of the Dharma, spoken so true— and the further you turn from it then the more tightly you strangle your chances for the higher realms, and ultimate good. Death will rip away your life, and the wrongdeeds you have done will dragyou to the lower realms, to a fearful place of mighty and savage suffering, to the fires. And so I ask you, where could you find any thought more disastrous for you than this idea, that what is impermanent could ever be permanent?\", \"wylie_method\": \"glyph-decode\", \"decode_score\": 1.0}"
      },
      {
        "id": 37136,
        "course": "SVN",
        "seq": 676,
        "acip": "JI LTAR ZHE NA, YID DU 'ONG BA LAS CHAGS PA DANG, YID DU MI 'ONG BA LAS ZHE SDANG DANG, DNGOS PO TZAM DU SGRO BTAGS PA LAS GTI MUG SKYE'O,,",
        "wylie": "ji ltar zhe na, yid du 'ong ba las chags pa dang, yid du mi 'ong ba las zhe sdang dang, dngos po tsam du sgro btags pa las gti mug skye'o",
        "english": "How does the venom rise? When they see something attractive, these people start to feel attachment. When they see something unattractive, they start to feel aversion. And when all they see is any single thing, they make it more than it ever was, and so give rise to dark ignorance.",
        "raw": "{\"acip\": \"JI LTAR ZHE NA, YID DU 'ONG BA LAS CHAGS PA DANG, YID DU MI 'ONG BA LAS ZHE SDANG DANG, DNGOS PO TZAM DU SGRO BTAGS PA LAS GTI MUG SKYE'O,,\", \"wylie\": \"ji ltar zhe na, yid du 'ong ba las chags pa dang, yid du mi 'ong ba las zhe sdang dang, dngos po tsam du sgro btags pa las gti mug skye'o\", \"english\": \"How does the venom rise? When they see something attractive, these people start to feel attachment. When they see something unattractive, they start to feel aversion. And when all they see is any single thing, they make it more than it ever was, and so give rise to dark ignorance.\", \"course\": \"SVN\", \"source_wave\": \"gmr-volumes-2026-08\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 9394,
        "course": "TCS02",
        "seq": 120,
        "acip": "DE LA SEMS SNYOMS PA NA MA LTA BU'I CHOS YID DU 'ONG BA'I SEMS CAN CIG DANG DGRA LTA BU'I CHOS YID DU MI 'ONG BA'I SEMS CAN CIG STE GNYIS MDUN DU GSAL BAR DMIGS NAS,",
        "wylie": "de la sems snyoms pa na ma lta bu'i chos yid du 'ong ba'i sems can cig dang dgra lta bu'i chos yid du mi 'ong ba'i sems can cig ste gnyis mdun du gsal bar dmigs nas",
        "english": "Once you've reached a sense of equanimity toward this person that you find unappealing, then move on to a new visualization.  This time picture two people sitting in front of you.  One is someone you find appealing to the extreme: someone like your mother.  The other is someone that you find unappealing to the extreme:  like your worst enemy.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"TCS02\", \"acip\": \"DE LA SEMS SNYOMS PA NA MA LTA BU'I CHOS YID DU 'ONG BA'I SEMS CAN CIG DANG DGRA LTA BU'I CHOS YID DU MI 'ONG BA'I SEMS CAN CIG STE GNYIS MDUN DU GSAL BAR DMIGS NAS,\", \"wylie\": \"de la sems snyoms pa na ma lta bu'i chos yid du 'ong ba'i sems can cig dang dgra lta bu'i chos yid du mi 'ong ba'i sems can cig ste gnyis mdun du gsal bar dmigs nas\", \"english\": \"Once you've reached a sense of equanimity toward this person that you find unappealing, then move on to a new visualization.  This time picture two people sitting in front of you.  One is someone you find appealing to the extreme: someone like your mother.  The other is someone that you find unappealing to the extreme:  like your worst enemy.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 17360,
        "course": "TCS13",
        "seq": 811,
        "acip": "DNGOS GZHI NI MAndAL GYI MJUG GI, BDAG GI CHAGS SDANG RMONGS GSUM SKYE BA'I YUL, ZHES SOGS KYI SKABS CHAGS PA SKYE YUL YID DU 'ONG BA DANG ,SDANG BA SKYE YUL YID DU MI 'ONG BA DANG, GTI MUG GI RIGS GYI YUL BAR MA RNAMS BLO YUL DU GSAL BTAB NAS MAndAL GYI STENG DU LTOS PA MED PAR PHUL NAS CHAGS SDANG ZHI BA'I GSOL 'DEBS BYAS NA LEGS SO,,",
        "wylie": "dngos gzhi ni maNDal gyi mjug gi, bdag gi chags sdang rmongs gsum skye ba'i yul, zhes sogs kyi skabs chags pa skye yul yid du 'ong ba dang ,sdang ba skye yul yid du mi 'ong ba dang, gti mug gi rigs gyi yul bar ma rnams blo yul du gsal btab nas maNDal gyi steng du ltos pa med par phul nas chags sdang zhi ba'i gsol 'debs byas na legs so",
        "english": "This actual practice occurs at the end of the secret world offering, at that point where we say, \"those objects which inspire in me attachment, anger and ignorance...\"27  Objects which inspire attachment are those which appear attractive.  Objects which lead us to anger are those which seem unpleasant.  And those objects which fall somewhere in between these two are those objects which invoke the perpetuation of our ignorance.  So in addition to our secret world offering, it is a powerful practice to pray for the death of our attachment and anger, by offering these objects without hesitation. _______________",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"TCS13\", \"acip\": \"DNGOS GZHI NI MAndAL GYI MJUG GI, BDAG GI CHAGS SDANG RMONGS GSUM SKYE BA'I YUL, ZHES SOGS KYI SKABS CHAGS PA SKYE YUL YID DU 'ONG BA DANG ,SDANG BA SKYE YUL YID DU MI 'ONG BA DANG, GTI MUG GI RIGS GYI YUL BAR MA RNAMS BLO YUL DU GSAL BTAB NAS MAndAL GYI STENG DU LTOS PA MED PAR PHUL NAS CHAGS SDANG ZHI BA'I GSOL 'DEBS BYAS NA LEGS SO,,\", \"wylie\": \"dngos gzhi ni maNDal gyi mjug gi, bdag gi chags sdang rmongs gsum skye ba'i yul, zhes sogs kyi skabs chags pa skye yul yid du 'ong ba dang ,sdang ba skye yul yid du mi 'ong ba dang, gti mug gi rigs gyi yul bar ma rnams blo yul du gsal btab nas maNDal gyi steng du ltos pa med par phul nas chags sdang zhi ba'i gsol 'debs byas na legs so\", \"english\": \"This actual practice occurs at the end of the secret world offering, at that point where we say, \\\"those objects which inspire in me attachment, anger and ignorance...\\\"27  Objects which inspire attachment are those which appear attractive.  Objects which lead us to anger are those which seem unpleasant.  And those objects which fall somewhere in between these two are those objects which invoke the perpetuation of our ignorance.  So in addition to our secret world offering, it is a powerful practice to pray for the death of our attachment and anger, by offering these objects without hesitation. _______________\"}"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "kind": "substring",
